1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Herod of Chalcis (d. 48 AD), also known as Herod V, was a son of Aristobulus IV, and the grandson of Herod the Great''', Roman client king of Judaea. He was the brother of Herod Agrippa I and Herodias. He was ve
2 CONC sted the rulership of Chalkis, a kingdom north of Judaea, as tetrarch. After the death of his brother, he was also given responsibility for the Temple in Jerusalem, as well as the appointment of the Temple's High Priest. Ananias w
2 CONC as appointed by him.[citation needed]
2 CONT
2 CONT His first wife was his cousin, Mariamne.[1] She bore him a son, who was also named Aristobulus, and who eventually became ruler of Chalcis.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Mariamne's death, he married his niece Berenice, with whom he had two sons, Berenicianus and Hyrcanus.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his death the kingdom was given to Herod Agrippa II.
2 CONT
