2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Herod of Chalcis=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Herod of Chalcis (d. 48-49 AD), also known as Herod V, (the Jewish Encyclopedia lists him as "Herod II") was a son of Aristobulus IV, and the grandson of Herod the Great, Roman client king of Judaea. He was the brother of Herod Ag
2 CONC rippa I and Herodias.
2 CONT
2 CONT His first wife was his cousin, Mariamne. She bore him a son named Aristobulus, who eventually became ruler of Chalcis ad Belum.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Mariamne's death, he married his niece Berenice, with whom he had two sons, Berenicianus and Hyrcanus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Around 41 AD, at the request of his brother, Herod Agrippa, emperor Claudius granted him the rule of Chalcis, a kingdom north of Judaea, as tetrarch. Three years later, after the death of his brother, he was also given responsibil
2 CONC ity for the Temple in Jerusalem, as well as the appointment of the Temple's High Priest. During the four years in which he exercised this right he appointed two high priests—Joseph, the son of Carnus, and Ananias was appointed by 
2 CONC him.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 48 AD. After his death the kingdom was given to Herod Agrippa II.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herod_of_Chalcis
