1 NOTE Almost converted by St. Paul
2 CONT
2 CONT Herod Agrippa II, King of Chalcis:
2 CONT
2 CONT Perhaps Agrippa saved Christianity when he decided not to put St. Paul to death and himself almost was converted by him to Christianity.
2 CONT In Acts 26, 27 Paul asks Herod Agrippa:
2 CONT " King Agrippa, believest thou the prophets? I know that thou believest. Then Agrippa said unto Paul, Almost thou persuadest me to be a Christian. And Paul said, I would to God, that not only thou, but also all that hear me this d
2 CONC ay, were both almost, and altogether such as I am, except these bonds. And when he had thus spoken, the king rose up, and the governor, and Bernice, and they that sat with them: And when they were gone aside, they talked between t
2 CONC hemselves, saying, This man doeth nothing worthy of death or of bonds."
