2 CONT To prevent Jewish violence from further escalating, Agrippa assembled the populace and delivered a tearful speech to the crowd in the company of his sister, but the Jews alienated their sympathies when the insurgents burned down t
2 CONC heir palaces. They fled the city to Galilee where they later gave themselves up to the Romans. Meanwhile, Cestius Gallus moved into the region with the twelfth legion, but was unable to restore order and suffered defeat at the bat
2 CONC tle of Beth-Horon, forcing the Romans to retreat from Jerusalem.
2 CONT
2 CONT Emperor Nero then appointed Vespasian to put down the rebellion, who landed in Judaea with fifth and tenth legions in 67. He was later joined by his son Titus at Ptolemais, who brought with him the fifteenth legion. With a strengt
2 CONC h of 60,000 professional soldiers, the Romans quickly swept across Galilee and by 69 marched on Jerusalem.
