2 CONT ==Was Mariamne Hasmonean's daughter's name Cypros or Mariamne?==
2 CONT
2 CONT *Cypros, according to Josephus ''The Antiquities of the Jews'', 18.130: Herod the Great had two daughters by Mariamne, the [grand] daughter of Hyrcanus; the one was Salampsio, who was married to Phasaelus, her first cousin, who wa
2 CONC s himself the son of Phasaelus, Herod’s brother, her father making the match; the other was '''Cypros, who was herself married also to her first cousin Antipater, the son of Salome, Herod’s sister'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Cypros, according to Wagner, Sir Anthony Richard; ‘Pedigree and Progress: Essays in the Genealogical Interpretation of History’
