2 CONT death 0054 AD, October 13 , in Rome, Italia, Roman Empire. · The ancient accounts are confused -- as is habitual in the cases of hidden and dubious deaths of emperors -- but their general drift is that Claudius was poisoned with a
2 CONC  treated mushroom, that he lingered a while and had to be poisoned a second time.
