1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Pheroras''' (Φερώρας; Pherṓras). Youngest son of Antipater [4], born c. 68 BC probably in Marissa (Idumaea), died c. 5 BC. His first marriage was to a Hasmonaean princess (the sister of Mariamme [1] I, the first
2 CONC  wife of his elder brother Herodes [1] I), his second was to a "slave girl" (Jos. BI 1,24,5; Jos. Ant. Iud. 16,7,3). P. was a close comrade-in-arms of his brother Herodes: on his commission he restored the fortress of Alexandreum 
2 CONC to the north of Jericho (Jos. Ant. Iud. 15,11,5; Jos. BI 1, http://referenceworks.brillonline.com/entries/brill-s-new-pauly/salome-e1028520?s.num=10
