1 NOTE Agrippina the Elder was one of the most virtuous and heroic women of hertime, born 12 B.C., died 33 A.D., daughter of Marcus Vipsanius Agrippa,the greatest military commander after Julius Caesar, and of Julia,daughter of Augustus.
2 CONC  She accompanied her husband, Caesar Germanicus, inhis military expeditions until his death at Antioch, 19 A.D. Herhusband's uncle, the Emperor Tiberius Claudius Caesar, jealous of theaffection of the people for Agrippina, banishe
2 CONC d her to a small island,where she died of hunger in 33 A.D.
2 CONT
2 CONT Agrippina the Elder, who married Germanicus. Agrippina the Elder andGermanicus had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Nero Julius Caesar, born 6 A.D. and died 30 A.D., married Julia,daughter of Drusus, son of Tiberius.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Drusus Julius Caesar, born 7 A.D. an died 33 A.D., married AemiliaLepida.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Gaius, born 12 A.D. and died 41 A.D., married Caesonia.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Agrippina the Younger, born 15 A.D. and died 59 A.D., married (1) Cn.Domitus Ahenobarbus, son of Antonia the Elder, daughter of Mark Antony,and her husband, L. Domitius Ahenobarbus, who died in 40 A.D. She married(3) Claudius. 
2 CONC The child from the first marriage was L. DomitiusAhenobarbus (afterwards Nero Claudius Caesar), born in 37 A.D. and diedin 68 A.D., infamous Roman Emperor (54 A.D.-68 A.D.), who succeededClaudius, who had ruled from 41 A.D. to 54 
2 CONC A.D. This Emperor Nerosupposedly "fiddled" while Rome burned to the ground. He married (1)Octavia, daughter of Claudius, and (2) Poppaea Sabina, who died in 65 A.D.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Drusilla.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Julia Livilla, following her mother's amorous traits, was banished(like her mother) by her grandfather, Emperor Caesar Augustus, to an islein the Adriatic, while her friend, Ovid, the poet, was banished to Tomiin the Black Sea.
