1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Aelia Paetina
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
2 CONT
2 CONT Aelia Paetina or Paetina was a Roman woman who lived in the 1st century, and was the second wife of the Emperor Claudius. Her biological father was consul of 4, Sextus Aelius Catus while her mother is unknown. She was born into th
2 CONC e family of the Aelii Tuberones, and thus apparently descended from the consul of 11 BC. Her father may have died when she was very young, as she was raised by her relative Praetorian Guard Prefect Lucius Seius Strabo (the biologi
2 CONC cal father of her adoptive brother or relative Lucius Aelius Sejanus, commander of the Praetorian Guard under the Emperor Tiberius).
2 CONT
2 CONT Aelia Paetina married the future Roman Emperor Claudius in 28, as his second wife. Their only child was their daughter Claudia Antonia, born in 30. Claudius divorced Paetina after October 31, after when her adoptive brother fell f
2 CONC rom power and was murdered. According to Suetonius, Claudius divorced Paetina for slight offences.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 48, after the death of Roman Empress and Claudius’ third wife Valeria Messalina, Claudius considered remarrying for the fourth time. Claudius’ freedman Tiberius Claudius Narcissus (who had in fact been the one who informed Clau
2 CONC dius that Messalina and her lover Gaius Silius were conspiring to kill him) supported a remarriage to Paetina. He suggested to Claudius to remarry her and reminded him they had a child together. Narcissus also stated that Paetina 
2 CONC would cherish Claudia Octavia and Britannicus, as well as Claudia Antonia. Claudia Octavia and Britannicus were Claudius’ children with Messalina.
2 CONT
2 CONT But another freedman, Gaius Julius Callistus, was against Claudius remarrying Paetina and stated to Claudius that he divorced her before; Callistus said that remarrying Paetina would make her more arrogant. Callistus suggested Lol
2 CONC lia Paulina, who had been Empress in AD 38 as the third wife of the Emperor Caligula (Claudius's nephew). The third Freedman, Marcus Antonius Pallas, recommended Claudius' niece, Agrippina the Younger, who also had a child from a 
2 CONC previous marriage, who was the future Emperor Nero. Agrippina was chosen, with dire implications for Claudius' own children: Antonia, Octavia, and Britannicus. Paetina's only child with Claudius, Claudia Antonia, died in AD 65 or 
2 CONC AD 66, shortly after the death of Nero's second wife Poppaea Sabina.
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás / Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aelia_Paetina
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Her birth's date refers to B.C. as well as Claudius I Caesar's and his other wives, refer to time B.C. (before Christ).
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p1625.htm#i48845
