2 CONT Flavius Josephus' The Jewish War Book 2, Chapter 5:
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Varus Composes The Tumults In Judea And Crucifies About Two Thousand Of The Seditious.''
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Thence he marched on to Jerusalem, and as soon as he was but seen by the Jews, he made their camps disperse themselves; they also went away, and fled up and down the country. But the citizens received him, and cleared themselve
2 CONC s of having any hand in this revolt, and said that they had raised no commotions, but had only been forced to admit the multitude, because of the festival, and that they were rather besieged together with the Romans, than assisted
2 CONC  those that had revolted. There had before this met him '''Joseph, the first cousin of [https://www.geni.com/people/Herod-Ethnarch-of-Samaria-Judaea-and-Edom/6000000003645877074 Archelaus]''', and Gratus, together with Rufus, who 
2 CONC led those of Sebaste, as well as the king's army: there also met him those of the Roman legion, armed after their accustomed manner; for as to Sabinus, he durst not come into Varus's sight, but was gone out of the city before this
2 CONC , to the sea-side. But Varus sent a part of his army into the country, against those that had been the authors of this commotion, and as they caught great numbers of them, those that appeared to have been the least concerned in th
2 CONC ese tumults he put into custody, but such as were the most guilty he crucified; these were in number about two thousand.
2 CONT
2 CONT Translation by William Whiston, https://www.josephus.org/works.htm
2 CONT
