2 CONT
2 CONT Cleopatra Selene II, Cleopatra VIII, Princess of Egypt, Ruler of Cyrenaica and Libya, was the fraternal twin to Alexander Helios, Prince of Egypt, born December 25, 40 BC, Alexandria, Egypt; died 6 AD.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Juba II, King of Numidia, circa 26 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cleopatra Selene II/Cleopatra VIII, Princess of Egypt, Ruler of Cyrenaica and Libya's eulogy by Epigrammatist Crinagoras of Mytilene:
2 CONT
2 CONT "The moon herself grew dark, rising at sunset,
2 CONT
2 CONT Covering her suffering in the night,
2 CONT
2 CONT Because she saw her beautiful namesake, Selene,
2 CONT
2 CONT Breathless, descending to Hades,
2 CONT
2 CONT With her she had had the beauty of her light in common,
2 CONT
2 CONT And mingled her own darkness with her death."
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: D. W. Roller, The World of Juba II and Kleopatra Selene (London 2003).
2 CONT
