1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT =Arcathius=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Arcathius (Greek: ο Άρκαθίας means in Greek ruler, flourished second half of 2nd century BC and first half of 1st century BC) was a Prince from the Kingdom of Pontus. He was a prince of Persian and Greek Macedonian ancestry. Arcat
2 CONC hius was among the sons born to King Mithridates VI of Pontus and his sister-wife Laodice. He was born and raised in the Kingdom of Pontus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arcathius joined his father’s generals Neoptolemus and Archelaus with 10,000 horses which he brought from Lesser Armenia at the commencement of the First Mithridatic War (89 BC–85 BC). He participated in the great battle fought ne
2 CONC ar the Amnias River in Paphlagonia which King Nicomedes IV of Bithynia was defeated.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a brilliant cavalry commander. In 86 BC, Arcathius invaded Macedonia with a separate army and completely conquered the country. He then proceeded to march against the Roman Dictator Lucius Cornelius Sulla, but on his way, A
2 CONC rcathius died near Mount Tisaion. Arcathius was a happy person in character and his father considered him as a beloved son and as a victorious hero in war.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source'''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arcathius
