2 CONT
2 CONT Lucius Caninius Gallus (fl. 1st century BC) was a Roman politician who served as consul in 37 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT A member of the Plebeian gens Caninia Gallus was the son of Lucius Caninius Gallus, and a grandson of Gaius Antonius Hybrida. Related to the triumvir Marc Antony, Gallus was probably elected to the office of Praetor by 40 BC at th
2 CONC e latest. He was then elected consul alongside Marcus Vipsanius Agrippa in 37 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gallus may have been a patron of the Latin poet Sextus Propertius.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
