2 CONT Cleopatra V of Egypt
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Cleopatra V Tryphaena of Egypt (Greek: Κλεοπάτρα, born c. 95 BC, died c. 69/68 BC or c. 57 BC) was a Ptolemaic Queen of Egypt. She is the only surely attested wife of Ptolemy XII.
2 CONT
2 CONT Descent and marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Cleopatra V may have been an illegitimate daughter of Ptolemy IX.[1] She is first mentioned in 79 BC in two papyri. In that year she married Ptolemy XII, king of Egypt. Ptolemy XII was also an illegitimate child of Ptolemy IX, but
2 CONC  it is unclear if he and Cleopatra V were full siblings or if they had different mothers. They received divine worship as theoí Philopátores kai Philádelphoi (father-, brother- and sisterloving gods).[2] In another theory she is l
2 CONC ikely to be a daughter of Ptolemy X Alexander because Cleopatra VII reveals her grandfather as Ptolemy X Alexander and that Strato confirms her sister Berenice's mother as Cleopatra V. In this case her mother could have been Beren
2 CONC ice III
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ID: I62181
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: Cleopatra V Tryphaena of Egypt
2 CONT
2 CONT Given Name: Cleopatra V Tryphaena
2 CONT
