2 CONT =Vipsania Polla=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Vipsania Polla was the daughter of Lucius Vipsanius Agrippa (a man of equestrian rank) and sister to another Lucius Vipsanius Agrippa, as well as the Roman general and politician Marcus Vipsanius Agrippa. Polla lived during the la
2 CONC te Roman Republic and during the reign of Rome's first Emperor Augustus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Although Polla was a distinguished woman, little is known of her life. She is remembered chiefly for overseeing construction of a monument called the Porticus Vipsania, a map of the Roman Empire engraved in marble. Marcus Agrippa 
2 CONC started the construction of this map before his death in 12 BC. The Porticus Vipsania was once displayed in Rome, not far from the Via Flaminia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Although the Porticus Vipsania has not survived, a description of it is given in Natural History by Pliny the Elder, and it is also known through the Peutinger Map.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vipsania_Polla
