2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopediaJump to:navigation, search 
2 CONT
2 CONT Aufidia or Alfidia (flourished 1st century BC), was a Roman Matron. Aufidia was a daughter to Roman Magistrate Marcus Aufidius Lurco and her mother is unknown. She was a member of the gens Aufidia, a Roman family of Plebs status, 
2 CONC who appeared in the Roman Republic and Roman Empire. They became a family of consular rank. Her father originally came from Fundi (modern Fondi, Italy).
2 CONT
2 CONT She married the future praetor, Marcus Livius Drusus Claudianus. They had at least two children: a daughter Livia Drusilla (58 BC-29) and a son Marcus Livius Drusus, who served as a Roman consul. Livia was to become the first Roma
2 CONC n Empress and third wife of the first Roman Emperor Augustus. Aufidia would be the maternal grandmother to Roman Emperor Tiberius Claudius Nero and Roman General Nero Claudius Drusus. The Roman Emperors Caligula, Claudius and Nero
2 CONC  were her direct descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source / Forrás:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aufidia
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Note: She married the future praetor, Marcus LIvius Drusus Claudianus. They had at least two children: a daughter Livia Drusilla (58 BC-29) and a son Marcus Livius Drusus, who served as a Roman consul. Livia was to become the firs
2 CONC t Roman Empress and third wife of the first Roman Emperor Augustus. Aufidia would be the maternal grandmother to Roman Emperor Tiberius Claudius Nero and Roman General Nero Glaudius Drusus. The Roman Emperors Caligula, Claudius an
2 CONC d Nero were her direct descendants.
