1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * from [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lollia_Saturnina '''Wikipedia'''], the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lollia Saturnina''' (c.10-41[1]) was a Roman noble woman that lived in the Roman Empire in the 1st century. She was the sister of the Roman empress Lollia Paulina[2] and was a mistress of the Roman emperor Caligula.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT =Family background and early life=
2 CONT
2 CONT Saturnina was a member of the plebeian gens Lollia. Saturnina was the first daughter of the suffect consul Marcus Lollius from the noble woman Volusia Saturnina[4] while her younger sister was Lollia Paulina.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father, Marcus Lollius was the son born to the Roman Politician and Military Officer Marcus Lollius[6] from his wife Valeria.[7] Valeria was one of the daughters of the literary patron, consul Marcus Valerius Messalla Corvinus
2 CONC  and a sister to the Roman Senators Marcus Valerius Messalla Messallinus and Marcus Aurelius Cotta Maximus Messalinus.[8] Her possible paternal uncle may have been Publius Lollius Maximus or at least a close relation to his patern
2 CONC al grandfather.[9] Publius Lollius Maximus was a soldier who served under the first Roman emperor Augustus;[10] later becoming a friend of the Poet Horace;[11] who became a possible poet, historian and must have been offered a pos
2 CONC t in the Retinue of the future Roman emperor Tiberius in about 20 BC.[12] Her cognomen Saturnina, she inherited from the paternal ancestry of her mother’s family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her mother Volusia Saturnina, came from an ancient and distinguished Senatorial family, that never rose above the Praetorship[13] which was of eques status.[14] She was the daughter of the prefect, Quintus Volusius from his wife C
2 CONC laudia. Her father served under Cicero in 51 BC to 50 BC in Cilicia[15] and was a pupil of his in oratory.[16] Claudia was a daughter of Pompey’s officer Drusus Claudius Nero and a sister of praetor, Tiberius Claudius Nero,[17] as
2 CONC  Volusia Saturnina was a first cousin to Roman emperor Tiberius and his brother, the General Nero Claudius Drusus.[18] The brother of Volusia Saturnina was the consul Lucius Volusius Saturninus.[19][20] Saturnina was born and rais
2 CONC ed in Rome. She was a beautiful woman,[21] who was one of the heirs of the wealth of her grandfather, Marcus Lollius.[22]
2 CONT
2 CONT =Marriage and Caligula=
2 CONT
2 CONT Saturnina married Decimus Valerius Asiaticus, who served as a suffect consul in 35[23] and was a wealthy, prominent Roman Senator.[24] Asiaticus was of Allobrogian origin from Gallia Narbonensis and was the first Roman Senator fro
2 CONC m that place.[25] Saturnina with Asiaticus had a son called Decimus Valerius Asiaticus.[26] There is a possibility they may had other children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Around 39, six months after Caligula divorced her sister Lollia Paulina, Saturnina became a mistress to Caligula. When Caligula started publicly discussing their relationship, which included in the presence of Asiaticus, this lead
2 CONC  him to hate Caligula.[27] The freedman Marcus Lollius Philippus, who loaned large sums of money to the various members of the gens, Sulpicii, may have been one of the freedmen of Saturnina.[28]
2 CONT
2 CONT =Inscriptional evidence=
2 CONT
2 CONT Below is a Latin inscription that has ever been found on Saturnina.[29] This inscription mentions one freedman Marcus Lollius Princeps and two freedwomen Lollia Urbana and Lollia Methe.[30]
2 CONT
2 CONT >D(is) m(anibus) s(anctum)|M(arco) Lollio Saturninae l(iberto)|Principi amico fidissimo|
2 CONT
2 CONT >qui vixit annis LVIII et|Lollia Saturninae l(ibertae)|Urbanae contubernal(i) eius [et]|
2 CONT
2 CONT >Lolliae Saturninae lib(ertae)|Methes sorori eius Lollia|C(aii) l(iberta) Galatea paren-
2 CONT
2 CONT >tib(us) carislsmis fecit permissu Urlsionis contuberanal(is) mei (CIL VI 21473a).
2 CONT
2 CONT =References=
