1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT =Vibia Aurelia Sabina=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Vibia Aurelia Sabina (170-before 217) was a Roman Princess. She was the youngest daughter and child born to Roman Emperor Marcus Aurelius and Roman Empress Faustina the Younger. She was a sister to Roman Empress Lucilla and Roman 
2 CONC Emperor Commodus. Her maternal grandparents were Roman Emperor Antoninus Pius and Roman Empress Faustina the Elder and her paternal grandparents were Domitia Lucilla and praetor Marcus Annius Verus.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Life'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Aurelia Sabina could have been born in Sirmium, Pannonia. In the year of her birth, her parents were preparing war expeditions at Sirmium. Aurelia Sabina was named in honor of the late Roman Empress Vibia Sabina, who was the wife 
2 CONC of the Roman Emperor Hadrian and her late father the distinguished suffect consul Lucius Vibius Sabinus. Vibia Sabina was a relative of her parents, as she was a great aunt to her parents who was half maternal sister to Rupilia Fa
2 CONC ustina. Rupilia Faustina was the paternal grandmother of Marcus Aurelius and the maternal grandmother Faustina the Younger.
2 CONT
2 CONT Throughout her childhood, Aurelia Sabina had travelled extensive with her parents throughout the Roman Empire. Sometime before her father died in 180 AD, Aurelia Sabina was betrothed to the African Roman Senator Lucius Antistius B
2 CONC urrus who came from Thibilis, a town near Hippo Regius in the Africa Province, whom she later married.
2 CONT
2 CONT When her parents died, her older brother Commodus succeeded her father as Roman Emperor in 180 AD. After Aurelia Sabina married Antistius Burrus in Rome, they returned and settled in Thibilis. In 181 AD, her husband served as an o
2 CONC rdinary consul there. In 188 AD, Antistius Burrus was involved in a conspiracy against Commodus.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was one of various Roman Senators in this conspiracy. When this conspiracy was uncovered, Antistius Burrus was put to death.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Prominent Italian resident in Roman Africa''
2 CONT
2 CONT But she was not involved and survived, remaining to live in Roman Africa.
2 CONT
2 CONT After her first husband had died, Aurelia Sabina married Lucius Aurelius Agaclytus, a Romano-Greek Freedman who was of Equestrian rank. Aurelia Sabina spent her remaining years in Thibilis. It appears from her marriages that she h
2 CONC ad no children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Due to her status; the status of her family and her connections, Aurelia Sabina became a prominent Italian resident in North Africa. According to surviving inscriptions found in Thibilis, Aurelia Sabina became an important "patron
2 CONC a" in Thibilis and the citizens of Thibilis made Aurelia Sabina an honorary citizen. Even the nearby romano-berber city of Calama was promoted to Roman colonia, while sponsored by Vibia Aurelia Sabina, sister of the Emperor Commod
2 CONC us. She was the official Roman Patrona of Calama.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vibia_Aurelia_Sabina
