1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gaius Asinius Quadratus Protimus or Gaius Protimus Quadratus Asinius ca. 165 - aft. 235 was the Proconsul of Achaea ca. 211 or in 220. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the brother of Gaius Asinius Rufus, son of Gaius Asinius Nicomachus and wife and cousin Julia Quadratilla or perhaps Asinia Marcellina, descendant of the family of Gaius Asinius Pollio and paternal grandson of Gaius Asinius
2 CONC  Rufus and wife Julia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married and was the father of Gaius Asinius Nicomachus Julianus, Proconsul of Asia between ca. 225 and ca. 230. 
