2 CONT =Marcus Asinius Agrippa=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Marcus Asinius Agrippa was Roman consul in 25 AD, and died at the end of the following year, 26 AD. He was also the half-brother of Julius Caesar Drusus, the natural son of the Emperor Tiberius. According to Tacitus, he was descen
2 CONC ded from a family more illustrious than ancient, and did not disgrace it by his mode of life, although he mentions no specifics. He was the grandson of Gaius Asinius Pollio, the second son of Gaius Asinius Gallus and Vipsania Agri
2 CONC ppina (after Gaius Asinius Pollio), and the father of Marcus Asinius Marcellus, who was consul in 54 along with Marcus Acilius Aviola, at the time the Emperor Claudius died.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
