1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://he.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%A0%D7%98%D7%99%D7%92%D7%95%D7%A0%D7%95%D7%A1_%D7%94%D7%A8%D7%90%D7%A9%D7%95%D7%9F  '''אנטיגונוס הראשון''']
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Antigonus''' was one of five sons of '''John Hyrcanus'''. During their father reign, he and his eldest brother '''Judah Aristobulus I''' cooperated in the war and the conquest of Samaria. After their father's death, Aristobulus
2 CONC  came into power, imprisoned his mother, killed her by starvation and executed all his brothers and their family members, except Antigonus, who became his illustrious military commander and served him faithfully. Nevertheless, Ari
2 CONC stobulus, whose health was rather poor was very suspicious of his brother's loyalty. He feared that his brother, a young military victorious commander might take his place and thus ordered that he must not visit him armed. He also
2 CONC  ordered that anyone who comes to the king Armed will be killed immediately.
2 CONT
2 CONT The queen who hated Antigonus ordered to inform him that his brother the king invites the victorious hero to present himself to the king in full arms. Antigonus accepted the invitation, and as expected, upon entering the royal pal
2 CONC ace fully armed, he was killed by the king's guards.
2 CONT
2 CONT The guilt over his brother's death intensified the king's sickness. It was said that he was coughing blood, bleeding on the same spot where his brother was killed.  This omen terrified the king, who eventually died of his sickness
2 CONC  and his guilt.
2 CONT
2 CONT Antigonus's greatest achievement while fighting on behalf of his brother was the occupation and conversion of the Itureans, a northern Arab/Arameic tribe in todays Lebanon area..
