1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ID: I62196 Name: Seleucus II of Syria Prefix: King Given Name: Seleucus II Surname: of Syria Nickname: Kallinikos Sex: M _UID: F4C739FBCA60BB429F28FE9FCC5394D90647 Change Date: 1 Jul 2005 Note: Seleucus II, called 
2 CONC Callinicus (circa 265-226 bc), ruler (247-226 bc) of the Seleucid kingdom, the son of Antiochus II Theos. Seleucus II was unable to prevent Ptolemy III of Egypt from invading Syria and Mesopotamia during the Third Syrian War (246-
2 CONC 241 bc). He allowed the Bactrians and Parthians to establish their independence in the east and lost his possessions in Asia Minor to his brother Antiochus Hierax.
