1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT =Antiochis=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT The name Antiochis, in Greek Ἀντιoχίς is the female name of Antiochus. Antiochis in Greek antiquity may refer to:
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Women'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Seleucid Princesses & Hellenistic Queen Consorts''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Antiochis, a daughter of Achaeus and granddaughter of Seleucus I Nicator. She married Attalus and became the mother of Attalus I, King of Pergamon
2 CONT * Antiochis, a sister of Antiochus III the Great, being a daughter of Seleucus II Callinicus and Laodice II. She married Xerxes of Armenia, King of Arsamosata, a city between the Euphrates and the Tigris
2 CONT * Antiochis, a daughter of Antiochus III the Great and Laodice III. She married Ariarathes IV of Cappadocia, and had one daughter and two sons by him
2 CONT * Antiochis, a daughter from the concubine of Antiochus IV Epiphanes. The cities of Tarsus and Mallus were given to her as a gift and the citizens of the cities revolted. Antiochus crushed the rebellion
2 CONT * Antiochis of Commagene, a daughter of Antiochus I Theos of Commagene
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Physician''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Antiochis of Tlos in Lycia, a 1st-century physician daughter of Diodotus (perhaps Diodotus the physician)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Athenian clan (phyle)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Antiochis, an Athenian Phyle was named Antiochis after Antiochus a mythical Attic hero. Aristides the just the son of Lysimachus, was of the tribe of Antiochis. For the subdivisions-townships of Antiochis in Attica, see deme.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antiochis
