1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT =Abdissares=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Abdissares ruled the kingdom of Sophene after the assassination of his father, Xerxes in 212 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are no known western sources for this king, only numismatic. His coins are almost similar to those of his father.
2 CONT
2 CONT His name seems to include the Aramaic prefix "Abd" which means slave. Aramaic was widely used in that region, and yet why would he have such a name, compared to his Armenian father Xerxes or brother Orontes IV? This may have seem 
2 CONC as a slur by the local Aramaic people, yet it is borne on his coins.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Ssares" sounds like Zareh (known in Greek sources as Zariadres), and it was Zareh who overthrew Abdissares in 200 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT These coups were the workings of king Antiochus III which also saw Zareh's son Artaxias (Artaxerxes) overthrow Orontes IV to become King of Armenia.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abdissares
