1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://he.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%9C%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8_%D7%94%D7%9E%D7%9B%D7%91%D7%99  '''אלעזר המכבי''' ] (ידוע גם כ'''אלעזר החורני''' וגם כ'''אלעזר אֲוָרָן''') היה בנו של מתתיהו החשמונאי ואחיו של יהודה המכב
2 CONC י. נודע בגלל מותו ההרואי בקרב בית זכריה במבצע התאבדות לחיסול פיל שחשב שעליו נמצא מנהיג האויב.
2 CONT
2 CONT מעט מאוד ידוע על אלעזר, מלבד סיפור מותו ההרואי. על פי מגילת אנטיוכוס, מתתיהו הכהן ראה בו את הקנאי שבאחים, דוגמת פנחס בן אלעזר הכהן. בספר חשמונאים ב' מסופר שאלעזר קרא לפני העם בספר הקודש לפני היציאה לקרב. הוא נקרא ה"חורני" מכיוון ש
2 CONC מקום מגוריו היה בית חורון.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleazar_Avaran '''Eleazar Avaran'''], also known as '''Eleazar Maccabeus''', '''Eleazar Hachorani'''/Choran(or Horani) (b. ???BCE - d. 162 BCE; Hebrew: אלעזר המכבי, אלעזר החורני Eleazar HaMakabi) was 
2 CONC the fourth son of Mattathias and the younger brother of Judas Maccabeus. He was killed at the Battle of Beth-zechariah during the Maccabean revolt. (1 Macc. 6:43-46)
2 CONT
2 CONT Very little is known About Eleazar, except his heroic death as was told. According to the scroll of Antichus, his father saw in him a Zealot among zealots, like Pinhas. In the book of 2 Maccabees it is told that Eleazar read from 
2 CONC the Tanakh in front of the people before going into his last battle. Contents
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Death'''
2 CONT
2 CONT According to 1 Maccabees, during the Battle of Beth-Zechariah, Eleazar identified a war elephant that he believed to carry the Seleucid King Antiochus V, due to the special armor the elephant wore. He decided to endanger his life 
2 CONC by attacking the elephant and thrusting a spear into its belly. The dead elephant then collapsed upon Eleazar, killing him as well. Despite this heroic effort, the smaller Jewish army was defeated in the battle. Josephus wrote tha
2 CONC t Eleazar, though killing many enemy soldiers, did not gain any real effect besides the name he made for himself. Another version of this story appears on the scroll of Antiochus, in which it is told that Eleazar was stamped on by
2 CONC  a horde of elephants.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Avaran'''
2 CONT
2 CONT All of the members of the family of Mattathias were given names aside from their given names in 1 Maccabees 2 (For example, Judas was given the name 'ha'Makabi', meaning 'the Hammer'.) Eleazar was given the name 'Avaran', which ha
2 CONC s been taken to mean 'the Piercer' (in reference to his death) or 'to be white' (referring to his light complexion.)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Commemoration'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleazar's death was a popular subject for art in the Middle Ages, where it was given a typological significance as prefiguring Christ's sacrifice of himself for mankind [3] The chance to portray an elephant was also welcomed by ar
2 CONC tists, although as most had never seen one, the results are often very strange. It is also portrayed in a painting of 19th century French artist Gustave Doré.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Israeli settlement Elazar in Gush Etzion, near the site of the battle of Beth-zechariah, is named after him. Also there are streets named after him in Jerusalem and in Tel Aviv.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikimedia Commons has media related to: [http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Eleazar_Maccabeus Eleazar Maccabeus]
