2 CONT Numerius Julius Caesar, the first of the Caesars lived about 300 B.C. Theword "Caesar" originally meant "a hairy head"; some say "an elephant."His son was Lucius Julius Caesar.
2 CONT
2 CONT Numerius Julius Caesar was the son of Lucius Julius Libo, who was the sonof Lucius Julius Libo. There was a gap of three generations separatinghim from Lucius Julius Julus, who was the son of Lucius Julius Julus, whowas the son of
2 CONC  Caius Julius Julus, who was the son of Caius Julius Julus,who was the son of Lucius Julius Julus, who was the son of NumeriusJulius Julus. There is then another gap of about 560 years separating himfrom Julus, who was the son of 
2 CONC Ascanius, who was the son of Aeneas,famous hero of The Iliad and The Aenead.
