2 CONT Ariobarzanes (in Greek Ἀριoβαρζάνης; reigned 266 BC-c. 250 BC) was the second king of Pontus, succeeding his father Mithridates I Ctistes in 266 BC and died in an uncertain date between 258 and 240. He obtained possession of the c
2 CONC ity of Amastris in Paphlagonia, which was surrendered to him. Ariobarzanes and his father sought the assistance of the Gauls, who had come into Asia Minor twelve years before the death of Mithridates, to expel the Egyptians sent b
2 CONC y Ptolemy II Philadelphus. Ariobarzanes was succeeded by Mithridates II.
2 CONT
