1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pompeia_Magna_(daughter_of_Sextus_Pompeius)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Pompeia Magna''' (about 42 BC - ?) was the daughter and only child of political rebel Sextus Pompey and Scribonia. Pompeia is only the child born to one of the sons of triumvir Pompey. Her paternal grandparents were Pompey and 
2 CONC Mucia Tertia. Her maternal grandparents were consul of 34 BC, Lucius Scribonius Libo and an unnamed woman from the gens Sulpicius, the family that the Roman Emperor Galba, had descended from his paternal side.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 39 BC, at the peace of Misenum, Sextus Pompey had betrothed Pompeia to Marcus Claudius Marcellus, the nephew to the heir of Roman Dictator Julius Caesar, Octavian and a son to Octavian’s elder sister Octavia Minor. Pompeia and 
2 CONC Marcellus in the end never married. She accompanied her father as they fled into Anatolia in 36 BC. After this moment, Pompeia is not mentioned again by the Roman ancient sources, though a list of female slaves owned by the Parthi
2 CONC an general Suren makes reference to "one Pompeia, a slave who rules her master, greatly cherished though poor and friendless."
2 CONT
