2 CONT http://ancienthistory.about.com/od/emperors/a/imperialdates.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Rome was originally the capital of the Roman emperor. Later, it moved to Milan, and then Ravenna (A.D. 402-476). After the fall of Romulus Augustulus, in A.D. 476, Rome continued to have an emperor for almost another millennium, b
2 CONC ut that Roman emperor ruled from the East.
2 CONT
2 CONT Julio-Claudians
2 CONT
2 CONT (31 or) 27 B.C. - 14 A.D. Augustus 14 - 37 Tiberius 37 - 41 Caligula 41 - 54 Claudius 54 - 68 Nero Year of the 4 Emperors
2 CONT
2 CONT (ends with Vespasian) 68 - 69 Galba 69 Otho 69 Vitellius
2 CONT
2 CONT Flavian Dynasty
2 CONT
2 CONT 69 - 79 Vespasian 79 - 81 Titus 81 - 96 Domitian 5 Good Emperors
2 CONT
2 CONT 96 - 98 Nerva 98 - 117 Trajan 117 - 138 Hadrian 138 - 161 Antoninus Pius 161 - 180 Marcus Aurelius (161 - 169 Lucius Verus)
2 CONT
2 CONT (The next cluster of emperors is not part of a specific dynasty or other common grouping, but includes 4 from the year of the 5 emperors, 193.) 177/180 - 192 Commodus 193 Pertinax 193 Didius Julianus 193 - 194 Pescennius Niger 193
2 CONC  - 197 Clodius Albinus
2 CONT
2 CONT Severans
2 CONT
2 CONT 193 - 211 Septimius Severus 198/212 - 217 Caracalla 217 - 218 Macrinus 218 - 222 Elagabalus 222 - 235 Severus Alexander (More emperors without a dynastic label, although it includes the year of the 6 emperors, 238.) For more on th
