2 CONT
2 CONT Antiochus I, called Soter (“the preserver”) (324-262 or 261 bc), king of Syria (280-262 or 261 bc). The second of the Seleucids, he was the son of Seleucus I, one of the generals and successors of Alexander the Great. In 275 bc An
2 CONC tiochus won a victory over the Galatians in Asia Minor but lost considerable territory to Ptolemy II. He was killed in battle during a war (263-261 bc) against Eumenes I (reigned 263-241 bc), ruler of Pergamum in Asia Minor.
