1 NOTE Antiochus I, called Soter ("the preserver") (324-262 or 261 bc), king of 
2 CONT Syria (280-262 or 261 bc). The second of the Seleucids, he was the son of 
2 CONT Seleucus I, one of the generals and successors of Alexander the Great. In 
2 CONT 275 bc Antiochus won a victory over the Galatians in Asia Minor but lost 
2 CONT considerable territory to Ptolemy II. He was killed in battle during a war 
2 CONT (263-261 bc) against Eumenes I (reigned 263-241 bc), ruler of Pergamum in 
2 CONT Asia Minor.
