2 CONT
2 CONT =Julia Caesaris (wife of Marius)=
2 CONT '''Julia Caesaris''' (ca. 130 BC – 69 BC) was a daughter of '''Gaius Julius Caesar II''' and '''Marcia''' (sister of consul Quintus Marcius Rex). She was a sister of Gaius Julius Caesar III (the father of Julius Caesar) and Sextus
2 CONC  Julius Caesar III. At about 110 BC she married Gaius Marius; as a result, she is sometimes referred to as Julia Maria.[citation needed] They had a son, Gaius Marius the Younger. According to Plutarch, it was by marrying her, a pa
2 CONC trician woman, that the up-start Marius got the snobbish attention of the senate and launched his political career[1]. Julia is remembered as a virtuous woman devoted to her husband and their only child. Her reputation alone permi
2 CONC tted her to keep her status, even after Sulla's persecutions against Marius himself and his allies. Julia Caesaris died in 69 BC and received a devoted funeral eulogy from her nephew Julius Caesar[2].
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Julia Caesaris=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Julia Caesaris (c. 130-69 BC) was a daughter of Gaius Julius Caesar II (praetor-grandfather of Caesar) and Marcia (daughter of praetor Quintus Marcius Rex). She was a sister of Gaius Julius Caesar III (the father of Julius Caesar)
2 CONC  and Sextus Julius Caesar III, consul in 91 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT At about 110 BC she married Gaius Marius; as a result, she is sometimes referred to as Julia Maria. They had a son, Gaius Marius the Younger.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Plutarch, it was by marrying her, a patrician woman, that the up-start Marius got the snobbish attention of the senate and launched his political career.[1] Julia is remembered as a virtuous woman devoted to her husba
2 CONC nd and their only child. Her reputation alone permitted her to keep her status, even after Sulla's persecutions against Marius himself and his allies.
2 CONT
2 CONT Julia Caesaris died in 69 BC and received a devoted funeral eulogy from her nephew Julius Caesar.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julia_Caesaris_(wife_of_Marius)
