2 CONT =Tiberius Sempronius Gracchus (consul 215 BC)=
2 CONT '''Tiberius Sempronius Tib. f. Tib. n. Gracchus''' (died 212 BC) was a Roman Republican consul in the Second Punic War. He was son of '''Tiberius Sempronius Tib. f. Gracchus''' who was apparently the first man from his branch to b
2 CONC ecome consul. Gracchus is first mentioned in 216 BC as curule aedile in which capacity he was inducted as Master of the Horse to the newly elected Dictator Marcus Junius Pera after the defeat at Cannae.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Family==
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife is unknown, but he had at least one son. Sempronius Gracchus's son '''Tiberius Sempronius Gracchus''' became a priest in 203 BC and died, while augur, in the plague in 174 BC. Lucius Manlius Acidinus Sempronianus, who rep
2 CONC laced the dead augur, may have been another son of this consul who had been adopted out into the patrician Manlii. The Tiberius Sempronius Gracchus who was exiled by Augustus for his affair with his daughter Julia may have been a 
2 CONC descendant.
2 CONT His brother '''Publius Sempronius Gracchus''' was the father of '''Tiberius Sempronius P.f. Tib.n. Gracchus''' whose sons '''Tiberius Gracchus''' and '''Gaius Gracchus''' were the famous reformers.
