2 CONC tween Seleucus I and Lysimachus, ending in the defeat and death of the latter, who was slain in battle in 281 BC, in the plain of Corius in Phrygia. Alexander conveyed his father's body to Lysimachia, to be buried in a tomb betwee
2 CONC n Cardia and Pactya, where it still stood in the time of Pausanias, four centuries later.
2 CONT
