2 CONT Philip II of Macedon, (Greek: Φίλιππος Β' ο Μακεδών — φίλος = friend + ίππος = horse[1] — transliterated  Philippos (help·info) 382 – 336 BC, was a Greek[2][3] king (basileus) of Macedon from 359 BC until his assassination in 336 
2 CONC BC. He was the father of Alexander the Great and Philip III.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents [hide]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Life
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 Assassination
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Marriages
