1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT =Quintus Pedius=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Quintus Pedius (died about 13) was a Roman painter and the first deaf person in recorded history known by name. He is the first recorded deaf painter and his education is the first recorded education of a deaf child. All that is k
2 CONC nown about him today is contained in a single passage of the Natural History by the Roman author Pliny the Elder.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pedius was the son of Roman Senator and orator Quintus Pedius Publicola, while his mother was an unnamed Roman woman. Pedius' paternal grandfather was the consul Quintus Pedius and his paternal grandmother was Valeria, a sister of
2 CONC  Roman Senator and orator Marcus Valerius Messalla Corvinus. His paternal grandfather Pedius and Roman emperor Augustus were maternal second cousins (or first cousins once removed if Pedius was the son of the elder Julia Caesaris 
2 CONC instead). Pedius was born deaf. On the advice of his paternal great-uncle Corvinus, and with permission from Augustus, Pedius was taught to paint. The boy turned out to be a talented painter, but died in his youth.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quintus_Pedius_(deaf_painter)
