2 CONT =Gaius Porcius Cato=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT Gaius Porcius Cato (2nd century BC) was the son of Marcus Porcius Cato Licinianus. Gaius was elected as a consul in 114 BC and assigned to the province of Macedonia and campaigned unsuccessfully against the Scordisci. He was accus
2 CONC ed of extortion in Macedonia, and was sentenced to pay a fine. He sought refuge[1] at Tarraco in Spain, and became a citizen of that town. This Gaius Porcius Cato was the father of Gaius Porcius Cato (tribune).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
