1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT =Nicomedes II of Bithynia=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicomedes II Epiphanes (Greek: Νικομήδης ὁ Ἐπιφανής) was the king of Bithynia from 149 to c. 127 BC. He was fourth in descent from Nicomedes I. Nicomedes II was the son and successor of Prusias II and Apame IV. His parents were re
2 CONC lated as they were cousins.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Life'''
2 CONT
2 CONT He was so popular with the people that his father sent him to Rome to limit his influence. However, in Rome, he also gained favor from the Roman Senate, forcing Prusias to send an emissary with secret orders to assassinate him. Bu
2 CONC t the emissary revealed the plot, and persuaded the prince to rebel against his father.
2 CONT
2 CONT Supported by Attalus II Philadelphus, king of Pergamon, he was completely successful, and ordered his father to be put to death at Nicomedia. During his long reign Nicomedes adhered steadily to the Roman alliance, and assisted the
2 CONC m against the pretender to the throne of Pergamon Eumenes III. He was succeeded by his son Nicomedes III.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicomedes_II_of_Bithynia
