2 CONT =Gnaeus Cornelius Cinna Magnus=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Gnaeus Cornelius Cinna Magnus (born between 47 BC and 35 BC) was the son of suffect consul Lucius Cornelius Cinna and Pompeia Magna. His sister was Cornelia Pompeia Magna.
2 CONT
2 CONT His maternal grandparents were Roman triumvir Pompey and Mucia Tertia, while paternal grandparents were consul Lucius Cornelius Cinna and an unnamed Roman woman. Cinna is the only grandson of Pompey, that has the name ‘Magnus’ and
2 CONC  is the only grandson that has partly his name.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cinna became a supporter to Roman triumvir Mark Antony. He was promoted to a priesthood. In 16 BC, Cinna and Aemilia Lepida, the granddaughter of triumvir Marcus Aemilius Lepidus were involved in a conspiracy against the Roman Emp
2 CONC eror Augustus. Cinna and Lepida were pardoned by the emperor, the first and last people to be pardoned after having been discovered to have conspired against him. This was famously the last documented conspiracy against Augustus. 
2 CONC Cinna served as a consul after 16 BC and is said to have been a close friend and advisor to Augustus until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cinna is the main character of a tragedy called Cinna by the famous 17th century French playwright Corneille.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gnaeus_Cornelius_Cinna_Magnus
