2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Archil, king of Iberia 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mihrdat_V_of_Iberia Mihrdat V, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mihrdat V (Georgian: მირდატ V, Latinized as Mithridates), of the Chosroid Dynasty, was the king of Iberia (Kartli, eastern Georgia) reigning, according to a medieval Georgian literary tradition, for 12 years, from c. 435 to 447 (a
2 CONC ccording to Cyril Toumanoff).
2 CONT
2 CONT Mihrdat was the son and successor of King Archil. The Georgian annals praise Mihrdat for his piety, but provide no details about his reign. He was married to Sagdukht, daughter of Barzabod, Mihranid prince of Gardman, and fathered
2 CONC  Vakhtang, his successor.[1]
2 CONT
