1 NOTE When Constantius was named caesar, or successor to the throne of the Roman 
2 CONT Empire, in 293, he divorced her because of her nonpatrician origin. She 
2 CONT devoted the rest of her life to religious pilgrimages, visiting Jerusalem 
2 CONT about 325 and founding there the Church of the Holy Sepulcher and the 
2 CONT Church of the Nativity. According to some legends, she was the discoverer 
2 CONT of the True Cross in Palestine. Her feast day is August 18.
