1 NOTE RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT Emperor of Rome; He married Marina Severa circa 345 (first wife).
2 CONT Emperor between 364 and 15 November 375. He set up residence, from which he
2 CONT directed operations against the invading Alemanni, in October 365 in Paris,
2 CONT France.3 He moved, to be in closer communication with his general Theodosius
2 CONT (father of the later Emperor Theodosius I) then defending Britain, and set up
2 CONT residence in 367 in Ambiani (modern Amiens), (France).3 He proclaimed his
2 CONT nine-year-old son, Gratian, as co-emperor on 24 August 367.3 He took up
2 CONT residence, where he remained for seven years devoting his attention to the
2 CONT construction of an elaborate system of fortifications on the Rhine, in October
2 CONT 367 in Trier, (Germany).3 He died on 17 November 375 in Bregetio, Pannonia
2 CONT Inferior, at age 54 years. Defending against an invasion of Pannonia by the
2 CONT Quadi, he went to Sirmium, where he fell sick and died.
