2 CONT Theodora (wife of Constantius I Chlorus) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Michael DiMaio, Jr. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Salve Regina University 
2 CONT
2 CONT Theodora was the eldest daughter, or perhaps stepdaughter, of Maximianus Herculius and his wife Eutropia . In order to strengthen the dynastic relationship between himself and Herculius when Maximianus Herculius appointed him as h
2 CONC is Caesar (junior emperor) in the west with the right of succession on 1 March 293, Constantius I put aside his wife Helena and married Theodora. She bore him six children: Flavius Dalmatius ,Julius Constantius ,Hannibalianus ,Con
2 CONC stantia ,Anastasia , and Eutropia .
