2 CONT 30The nature of Maximus' command at the time of his revolt is a matter of great controversy. He is normally identified as one of the comes Britanniarum , the dux Britanniarum or the comes litoris Saxonici . See Birley (1981), 346-
2 CONC 52. I suspect that he was the vicarius of the magister peditum praesentalis Merobaudes and that he commanded a small expedition to Britain ca . 382 similar to that which Theodosius had led there in 367/68.
