2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Titus Pomponius=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Titus Pomponius was a member of the Gens Pomponia and a direct descendant in male line of Pomponius, the first son of Numa Pompilius, the second King of Rome, and came from an old but not strictly noble Roman family of the equestr
2 CONC ian class. He was the owner of an excellent library in his house at the Appian Way, lord of a great fortune, partner of many companies of publicans and of important companies of fishing and conserves (essentially garum) in Gades, 
2 CONC in Hispania, and of great properties in Illyricum.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married to Caecilia Metella (ca 130-ca 50 BC), the sister of Quintus Caecilius Metellus, he was the father of Titus Pomponius Atticus and Pomponia, married about 70 BC to Quintus Tullius Cicero (102 BC – 43 BC), brother of the cel
2 CONC ebrated orator Marcus Tullius Cicero.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
