2 CONT =Pomponia=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Pomponia was a Roman woman who flourished in the first century BC and was an only sister to Cicero’s friend the Roman Kinght Titus Pomponius Atticus. She was an aunt to Titus Servilius Pomponianus, Caecilia Attica and a great-aunt
2 CONC  to Vipsania Agrippina (first wife to future Roman Emperor Tiberius).
2 CONT
2 CONT Cicero through his effective mediation was able to arrange for Pomponia to marry his younger brother Quintus Tullius Cicero. Quintus and Pomponia married in 68 BC. Pomponia bore Quintus a son of the same name.
2 CONT
2 CONT Quintus and Pomponia had a long unhappy marriage and they constantly quarrelled. Pomponia was a woman of strong character. Their constant quarrelling greatly upset Cicero and he mentioned this in his letters to Atticus. Cicero tri
2 CONC ed to assist his sister-in-law and his brother to resolve their problems, but Cicero naturally supported his brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT When the younger Quintus Tullius Cicero grew up, he tried (encouraged by his uncles) to reconcile his parents, but was unsuccessful. Pomponia and the elder Quintus divorced in later 45 BC or early 44 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT In December 43 BC, Cicero, Quintus, and Quintus minor were executed on the orders of Roman Triumvir Mark Antony.
2 CONT
2 CONT As an act of decency, Antony handed over Philologus, a former slave and traitor to Cicero, to Pomponia. According to Plutarch, Pomponia punished Philologus for his treachery with terrible punishments, which included forcing him to
2 CONC  cut off pieces of his own flesh, then roasting and eating them.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pomponia#Sister_of_Titus_Pomponius_Atticus
