2 CONT
2 CONT '''Justa Grata Honoria''', commonly referred to during her lifetime as '''Honoria''', was the older sister of the Western Roman Emperor [https://www.geni.com/people/Valentinian-III-Western-Roman-Emperor/6000000002119493371 Valenti
2 CONC nian III] — famous for her plea of love and help to  [https://www.geni.com/people/Attila-Scourge-of-God-59th-King-of-the-Huns/6000000000722248117 Attila the Hun], which led to his proclamation of his claim to rule the Western Roma
2 CONC n Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT She offered herself in marriage to Attila the Hun, who demanded the western half of the Roman Empire as her dowry. As a result, her brother put her under close guard and married her to a senator, and Attila invaded the Empire in 4
2 CONC 51 and 452.
2 CONT
2 CONT Coins attest that she was granted the title of Augusta not long after the ascension of her brother in 426.
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justa_Grata_Honoria
