1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was Praefectus Praetorio Galliarum (418 CE), and Consul of Rome (421 CE). He was probably a descendant of Philagrius, patricius, and perhaps of Lucius Maecilius, leader of the plebeians in Rome 471 BCE.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Flavius Julius Agricola (365 – after 421) was a Consul of Rome in 421. He was perhaps the father of Avitus, another son who was the father of [http://www.geni.com/people/Papianilla-Avita/6000000007337427221 Papianilla], wife of [h
2 CONC ttp://www.geni.com/people/Tonantius-Ferreolus-II/6000000007337035804 Tonantius Ferreolus], and a daughter, born in 385, married to Flavius Felix, born in 380, a son of Ennodius, Proconsul of Africa, who might have been Flavius Con
2 CONC stantius Felix (380 – 430), Consul of Rome in 428, who married Padusia and was an ancestor of Felix, Consul in 511.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT From French Wikipedia
2 CONT https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agricola_(consul_en_421)
2 CONT
2 CONT Il se marie avec Magna Constantina, décédée en Rome, et eut trois filles et deux fils:
2 CONT 1. Padusia Flavia Agricola, mariée avec Flavius Constantius Felix ;
2 CONT 2. Eparchius Avitus, empereur d'Occident ;
2 CONT 3. Eparchia Avita Agricola, mariée avec Alcimus Apollinaris ;
2 CONT 4. Eparchia Avita Palladia, mariée avec Flavius Anicius Petronius Maximus ; et
2 CONT 5. Ommatius Agricola (peut-être son neveu paternel), fl. av. 400-ap. 468, sénateur d'Arverne, père de Papianilla Agricola, femme de Tonantius Ferreolus, et de Hiberia, femme de Rurice de Limoges.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
