1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Titus Annius Milo==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Titus Annius Milo''' (died 48 BC) was a Roman political agitator. The son of Gaius Papius Celsus, he was adopted by his maternal grandfather, Titus Annius Luscus. In 52 BC, he was prosecuted for the murder of Publius Clodius Pu
2 CONC lcher and exiled from Rome. He was unsuccessfully defended by his friend, Marcus Tullius Cicero, in the speech Pro Milone. 
2 CONT
