1 NOTE Pompeia Magna (born between 80 BC and 75 BC - before 35 BC) was the only daughter and second child born to Roman triumvir Pompey the Great or Gnaeus Pompeius Magnus from his third marriage to Mucia Tertia. Her eldest brother is Gn
2 CONC aeus Pompeius an
2 CONT d her younger brother is Sextus Pompeius.
2 CONT Pompeia was born and raised in Rome. In 59 BC, Pompey had married Julia Caesaris, the daughter of Julius Caesar, as his fourth wife. Julia before marrying her father was betrothed to politician Quintus Servilius Caepio, likely the
2 CONC  Brutus who late
2 CONT r assassinated Caesar. After Pompey and Julia had married, Pompeia was betrothed to Quintus Servilius Caepio , but in the end she didn’t marry Caepio, instead Pompeia married Faustus Cornelius Sulla , a politician who was the son 
2 CONC of Roman dictato
2 CONT r Lucius Cornelius Sulla from his wife Caecilia Metella. Pompeia bore Faustus three children (they are listed below). Around 47 BC, Faustus had died in the African War against Julius Caesar. Her two sons fell into the hands of Jul
2 CONC ius Caesar, howe
2 CONT ver Caesar dismissed them and pardoned them.
2 CONT After 46 BC, Pompeia married for a second time to politician Lucius Cornelius Cinna, who was brother of Julius Caesar’s first wife Cornelia Cinna minor and the maternal uncle of Caesar’s late daughter with Cornelia, Julia Caesaris
2 CONC . Pompeia bore C
2 CONT inna two children (they are listed below).
2 CONT For a time Pompeia, had accompanied her younger brother Sextus Pompeius to Sicily. It was in Sicily, that Pompeia made various presents for the younger future Roman Emperor Tiberius, who fled with his parents there from the Second
2 CONC  Triumvirate. Po
2 CONT mpeia gave Tiberius as presents a cloak, a brooch and some gold plaques. The historian Suetonius, states that these presents were preserved and were exhibited in Baiae, in his time. Her younger brother survived Pompeia as she died
2 CONC  before 35 BC.
2 CONT editPompeia’s Marriages and Children
2 CONT
2 CONT First marriage to Faustus Cornelius Sulla, a politician who was the son of Roman dictator Lucius Cornelius Sulla from his wife Caecilia Metella. Child:
2 CONT Faustus (II) Cornelius Sulla
2 CONT Second marriage to politician Lucius Cornelius Cinna, which was the former brother-in-law of Julius Caesar. Pompeia’s children with Cinna were:
2 CONT Gnaeus Cornelius Cinna Magnus
2 CONT Cornelia Pompeia Magna who married Lucius Scribonius Libo consul of 16
