2 CONT
2 CONT Flavius Felix (died 430) was a politician of the Western Roman Empire, who reached the prominent rank of patrician before being killed by order of Flavius Aetius. For his consulate, in 428, he issued some consular diptychs, one of
2 CONC  which has been preserved until modern times.
