1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Flavius Magnus''' (c. 390 or 405 – 475) was a powerful politician in Gaul, where he was widely respected for his integrity and practical wisdom during the late age of the Western Roman Empire. He was a Roman Sen
2 CONC ator of Narbonne (then Narbo), Consul of Rome with Flavius Apollonius in 460 and the Prefect of Gaul in 469.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Family
2 CONT
2 CONT His father, born ca 380, might have been the son of Ennodius, Proconsul of Africa. He might have been Flavius Felix (380 – 430), Consul of Rome in 428, who married Padusia and was allegedly an ancestor of Felix, Consul in 511. His
2 CONC  mother (b. 385) was a daughter of Flavius Julius Agricola, Consul of Rome in 421 and father of Emperor Avitus.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the father of:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Magnus Felix (430 – after 469), a Patron in 469, married to Attica (b. 440), perhaps the parents of:
2 CONT
2 CONT           o a son or a daughter (b. 460 or 465), who begot:
2 CONT
2 CONT                 + Flavius Arcadius Placidus Magnus Felix, Consul of Rome in 511
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Araneola (b. 435 or 440), married to Polemius, perhaps them the parents of:
2 CONT
2 CONT           o a son or a daughter (b. 460 or 465), who begot:
2 CONT
2 CONT                 + Flavius Arcadius Placidus Magnus Felix, Consul of Rome in 511
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Flavius Probus, a Roman Senator
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Ennodius (perhaps) (CRP 458), the father of Cynegia?
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources and references
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Sidonius Apollinaris, The Letters of Sidonius (Oxford: Clarendon, 1915), pp. clx-clxxxiii
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Christian Settipani, Les Ancêtres de Charlemagne (France: Éditions Christian, 1989).
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Christian Settipani, Continuite Gentilice et Continuite Familiale Dans Les Familles Senatoriales Romaines A L'epoque Imperiale, Mythe et Realite, Addenda I - III (juillet 2000- octobre 2002) (n.p.: Prosopographica et Genealo
2 CONC gica, 2002).
2 CONT
