2 CONT Suffix : Kung av Köln 
2 CONT
2 CONT Anmärkning: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mördad av sin egen son på inrådan av Clovis I, kung av theFranks . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Känd under smeknamnet " lama " , han var en av flera frankishkings , hans rike är i Rhenlandet . När CLOVIS wasconsolidating sin makt som ensam kung över frankerna, Sigibert wasprobably hans starkaste rival. Det verkar som om två 
2 CONC kungen var onfriendly villkor. Sigebert son, CLODERIC , även slogs med CLOVIS inhis kampanj mot visigoterna . Som närstående av Edward James i hisbook , " Frankerna ":" CLOVIS övertalade CLODERIC att döda sin far Ashe gick i skoge
2 CONC n utanför Köln. Medan CLODERIC wasselecting sin belöning från sin fars skattkista , dela en av CLOVIS'Franks hans skalle med en yxa . CLOVIS meddelade till RhinelandFranks att CLODERIC dödat sin far och hade i sin tur beenkilled ,
2 CONC  de rök ihop sina sköldar , ropade deras godkännande, och madeCLOVIS sin konung . "
2 CONT
2 CONT Eftersom den merovingiska dynastin utvecklades , den separata identiteter ofNeustria (hem för Saliska franker ) och Austrasien ( hem theRipuarian Franks ) bibehölls.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigobert_the_Lame
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sigobert the Lame (also Sigibert or Sigebert) (died ca. 509) was a king of the Franks in the area of Zülpich (Latin: Tolbiac) and Cologne. He was presumably wounded at the knee at the Battle of Tolbiac against the Alamanni. Accord
2 CONC ing to Gregory of Tours, he was murdered by his son Chlodoric upon the instigation of Clovis I, sometime after his victory on the Visigoths (507). Clovis then accused Chlodoric of murder and had him killed in his turn. In this way
2 CONC  Clovis became king of Sigobert's and Chlodoric's people. Gregory suggests that Chlodoric was murdered in the same campaign that also killed the Frankish King Chararic. Before, Clovis had killed Ragnachar and his brothers. After a
2 CONC ll these murders Gregory tells us that Clovis lamented that he had left no family anymore, implying that amongst his own casualties were close relatives.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~pinegar/WC03/WC03_044.HTM
2 CONT
2 CONT * Father: Chlodebaud King Of Koeln (ca0430 - 0483)  
2 CONT * Mother: Amalaberge (ca0435 - ca0478) 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sigebert "Le Boiteux" K. Of Koeln=
2 CONT b.;  d. ca 0508; bur.; occ. Reigned 496 - 508
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT > Cloderic King < 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sigibert de Cologne, dit "le boiteux" règne sur les Francs ripuaires autour des années 500, dans le Haut Moyen Âge.
2 CONT Il se bat à Tolbiac contre les Saliens. Il boitait en raison d'un pied malade rapporte Grégoire de Tours. Selon Grégoire de Tours, il meurt assassiné par son propre fils, à l'instigation de Clovis, dans la forêt de Buconia, qu'on 
2 CONC suppose située près de Cologne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son royaume constitue un noyau de la future Austrasie. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigebert_of_Cologne
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Murdered by his son. Called The Lame because he injured his knee in battle.
2 CONT --------------------
