1 NOTE AFN:9GBK-CJ
1 NOTE
2 CONT from &quot;Our Folk&quot; by Albert D Hart, Jr.
1 NOTE "According to a tradition accepted at the Court of Charlemagne, Saint Arnulf, who had been appointed Bishop of Metz by royal favour, was descended from the family of Ferreolus, one of the great houses of the most Romanised provinc
2 CONC e of Gaul - the Narbonnaise.  His father, Ansbert, who was of senatorial rank, had married Blithilda, one of the daughters of Clotar I.  We have already observed that Saint Begga, the mother of Pepin d'Heristal, was the daughter o
2 CONC f a Gallo-Roman.  Thus the family into which Charlemagne was to be born had as much Roman and Gallo-Roman as German blood in its veins; ..."
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference Documentation Includes
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.) Fr. Funck-Brentano, A History of Gaul, Celtic, Roman and Frankish Rule (Barnes & Noble New York 1993).
