1 NAME Flavius Probus
2 GIVN Flavius Probus
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 440
2 PLAC Narbonne, Aude, Languedoc-Roussillon, France
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 469
2 PLAC Gaul, , , France
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Gallo-Roman Senator, v. nob. (vir nobilis), senateur romain à Narbonne
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Flavius Probus (born ca 420, 430 or 435), a Roman Senator and a v. nob. (vir nobilis) of Narbonne, then Narbo, was a man of literary taste and precocious ability. His father was Flavius Magnus, Consul of Rome in 46
2 CONC 0. He was a friend of Sidonius Apollinaris from their schooldays.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married before 450 Eulalia (?), born ca 425, a cousin of Sidonius Apollinaris, daughter of Thaumastus. They were perhaps the parents of:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Industria of Narbonne, then Narbo, born ca 450 or 465, married before 475 to Tonantius Ferreolus
2 CONT * Firminus (455 or 460 – ca 503), v. inl. at Arles, then Arelate, and a propinq. of Ennodius
2 CONT * Probatius (certain son), Bishop of Uzès in 506
2 CONT
2 CONT References and sources
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sidonius Apollinaris, The Letters of Sidonius (Oxford: Clarendon, 1915), pp. clx-clxxxiii
2 CONT * Christian Settipani, Les Ancêtres de Charlemagne (France: Éditions Christian, 1989).
2 CONT * Christian Settipani, Continuite Gentilice et Continuite Familiale Dans Les Familles Senatoriales Romaines A L'epoque Imperiale, Mythe et Realite, Addenda I - III (juillet 2000- octobre 2002) (n.p.: Prosopographica et Genealogica
2 CONC , 2002).
2 CONT
