1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Alcimus Ecdicius Avitus''' (c. 470 – February 5, 523) was a Latin poet and archbishop of Vienne in Gaul.
2 CONT
2 CONT Avitus was born of a prominent Gallo-Roman senatorial family in the kinship of Emperor Avitus.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Ford Mommaerts he was son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Saint-Hesychius-I-Bishop-of-Vienne/6000000000312820005 Saint Hesychius of Vienne] and his wife [http://www.geni.com/people/Audentia/6000000005747722273 Audentia
2 CONC ]. 
