1 NOTE From THE RUFUS PARKS PEDIGREE by Brian J.L. Berry, chart pg 61.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 65:
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.     GUNDIAC, A. 436-73, Burgundian king, settled his surviving followers in the Savoy and became an ally of the romans.  He was recognized as Master of the Soldiers or Commander-in-Chief.  He mar. a sister of Ricimer the Empero
2 CONC r Maker.   She was granddaughter of WALLIA  the Visigothic king who settled his Germanic people in Gaul 418.  GUNDIAC had three sons, all Burundian kings.  The eldest, Gundobad, killed his brother CHILPèRIC II.  Godigisil the youn
2 CONC gest, allied himself with CLOVIS the Salic but was executed 500 by Gundobad after a battle at Vienne.
2 CONT
2 CONT !Availability: The libraries of Ken, Karen, Kristen, Kevin, Brian, Amy, Adam and FAL
