1 NOTE {geni:about_me} b)         THEUDERADA (-after 690).  Paulus Diaconus records that "Grimualdus rex…suo filio Romualdo" married "Lupo duce…filiam eius Theuderadam" after her father's death[196].  "Theuderada" is named wife of Duke R
2 CONC omuald in the Benedicti Chronicon, but her origin is not given[197].  Romuald married her after her father, who had rebelled against King Grimoald, was killed.  She was regent in 690 during the minority of her son Duke Gisulf[198]
2 CONC .  
