2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
2 CONT
2 CONT Flavius Areobindus Dagalaiphus (ca 460 - 546) was Magister Militum from 503 to 504 and Roman Consul in 506. He was a son of Flavius Dagalaiphus (ca 430 - aft. 461), Roman Consul in 461, and wife Godisthea (b. ca 445).
2 CONT
2 CONT He married in 479 Anicia Juliana (Constantinople, 462 - 527/528), daughter of Emperor Olybrius and wife Placidia, and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT Areobindus (b. ca 485), a Pagan, married to Georgia and had: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Probus (ca 510 - 542), married to Aviena (b. ca 520), daughter of Rufius Magnus Faustus Avienus (ca 485 - 534/545), Roman Consul in 502, and wife Barbara (b. ca 495), and had issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Flavius Anicius Olybrius Iunior (ca 480 - aft. 524/aft. 527), Roman Consul in 491
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás / Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flavius_Areobindus_Dagalaiphus
