1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Eulalia''' (c435-?), wife of '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Flavius-Probus/6000000005794548458 Probus]'''. She was a cousin-german of '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Saint-Sidonius-Apollinarius-Bishop-of-Clermont
2 CONC /6000000009437556787 Sidonius]''', and a daughter of '''[http://www.geni.com/people/Thaumastus-I-Praetorian-Prefect-of-Gaul/6000000005796266210 Thaumastus]'''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Christian Settipani, [http://francia.digitale-sammlungen.de/Blatt_bsb00016294,00213.html?prozent=1 Ruricius Ier évêque de Limoges et ses relations familiales] in ''Francia'' 18/1 (1991), 203.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT Thaumastus (born c. 400)[1] was a friend and uncle of Sidonius Apollinaris. His brother, the elder Apollinaris was born around 405[2] and was the praetorian prefect of Gaul under Valentinian III between 425 and 455.[3] Thaumastus 
2 CONC and his brother were both sons of another Apollinaris, praetorian prefect of Gaul before 409[3] and were friends with his successor Decimus Rusticus. Thaumastus was associated with Tonantius Ferreolus in the impeachment of Arvandu
2 CONC s[4]. He was the father of '''Eulalia, born in 425[2], married before 450 to Flavius Probus, Roman Senator'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thaumastus
