2 CONT http://gw2.geneanet.org/index.php3?b=lrenouard&lang=fr;p=gondahar+ou+gondichar;n=de+burgondie <nowiki>--------------------</nowiki> About Gundahar I Gjukungar, Leader of the Burgundians He led the Burgundians across the Rhine in t
2 CONC he early 5th century, establishing a kingdom at Worms. The Romans transferred control of the stronghold of Worms—which they called Augusta Vangionum—to the Burgundians, a Germanic tribe immortalized in the Nibelungenlied, or Song 
2 CONC of the Nibelungs. King of the Burgunds in Worms, between 413 and 436. Killed in battle against the Huns and Aëtius. This is part of the 12th-century German epic "Nibelungenlied." He became a hero of medieval legends.
