2 CONT 1.   GUNDICAIIRE (GUNDAHAR), c.385-k. 437, Burgundian king.  In 435 taking advantage of Roman weakness, he led his people in an invasion of Upper Belgica (Trier, Metz).  But in 437 the Roman general Aetius induced his friends the 
2 CONC huns to attack and crush them.  Thousands were slain including GUNDICAIRE.
