2 CONT
2 CONT m '''MENIA''' ---.  The Historia Langobardorum names "mater…Audoin…Menia uxor fuit Pissæ regis"[149].  This wording suggests that "Pissæ regis" was not the father of Audoin, presumably Menia's [https://www.geni.com/people/Menia-s-
2 CONC 2nd-husband/6000000184644422159 second husband].  It is assumed that "Pissæ" indicates that he was king of a tribe of that name. 
2 CONT
