2 CONT Inventor of the screw and screwpump.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nebuchadnezzar II (Aramaic: ܢܵܒܘܼ ܟܘܼܕܘܼܪܝܼ ܐܘܼܨܘܼܪ ‎; English pronunciation: /nɛbəkədˈnɛzər/  ( listen); Arabic: بختنصر c 634 – 562 BC) was king of the Neo-Babylonian Empire, who reigned c. 605 BC – 562 BC. According to the Bible
2 CONC , he conquered Judah and Jerusalem, and sent the Jews into exile. He is credited with the construction of the Hanging Gardens of Babylon and the destruction of the First Temple. He is featured in the Book of Daniel and is also men
2 CONC tioned in several other books of the Bible.
2 CONT ---------------------------------
2 CONT
