2 CONT
2 CONT '''Kashshaya''' (Akkadian: Kaššaya)[94] – attested in several economic documents from Nebuchadnezzar's reign as "the king's daughter".[95] Her name is of unclear origin; it might be derived from the word kaššû (kassite).[96] Kashs
2 CONC haya is attested from contemporary texts as a resident of (and landowner in) Uruk.[30] Kashshaya is typically, although speculatively, identified as the daughter of Nebuchadnezzar who married Neriglissar.[88][97]
