2 CONT >>>'''[https://www.geni.com/people/Chlodomir-I-King-the-Franks-at-Orl%C3%A9ans/6000000010395927288?through=6000000005913350166 CHLODOMER] ([494/95]-killed in battle Vézeronce 21 Jun 524).  Gregory of Tours names Chlodomer as secon
2 CONC d son of King Clovis and his wife Clotilde[102].  "Theodorico, Chlomiro, Hildeberto, Hlodario" are named (in order) as sons of "Chlodoveus" in the Regum Merowingorum Genealogia[103].  He succeeded his father in 511 as CHLODOMER Ki
2 CONC ng of the Franks, at Orléans, his territory covering the Loire valley from Orléans to Tours, Chartres, Sens and Auxerre.  Gregory of Tours records that Chlodomer's mother incited him to attack Burgundy to avenge the death of her p
2 CONC arents.  He defeated and captured Sigismond King of Burgundy in his first invasion, but was defeated and killed by Sigismond's brother Gondemar during a second invasion[104].  The Liber Historiæ Francorum records that "Chlodomiris
2 CONC " led an army into Burgundy against "Godmarum", a marginal additional recording that "Gladmirus filius Clodovei regis Francorum" was killed during the course of the attack[105].  m ([514] or 521) as her first husband, [https://www
2 CONC .geni.com/people/Guntheuca-of-the-Burgundians-Queen-of-Orl%C3%A9ans/6000000007217837471?through=6000000010395927288 GUNTHEUCA] [Gondioque], daughter of - [King of Burgundy].  Gregory of Tours names Guntheuc as widow of King Chlodo
2 CONC mer and records her second marriage with his brother Clotaire, but does not give her origin[106].  The Liber Historiæ Francorum records that "Chlotharius" married "uxorem fratris sui…Gundeucam"[107].  Settipani suggests, for onoma
2 CONC stic reasons only, that she may have belonged to the Burgundian royal family which, if correct, means that she may have been the daughter of either King Gondebaud or his brother Godogisel[108].  However, Gregory makes no mention o
2 CONC f this in his lengthy description of King Chlodomer's campaigns in Burgundy, an omission which is surprising if the king’s wife was related to his opponents.  She married secondly ([524]) as his first wife, Clotaire I [Chlothachar
2 CONC /Lothar] King of the Franks.  King Chlodomer & his wife had three children: [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MEROVINGIANS.htm#ClovisIB MEDLANDS]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>a)        [https://www.geni.com/people/Theodebald-Merovingian/6000000037864821289?through=6000000010395927288 THEODEBALD] ([521]-murdered Paris 531, bur Paris, basilique des Saints-Apôtres [later église de Sainte-Geneviève]). 
2 CONC  Gregory of Tours names (in order) Theudovald, Gunthar and Chlodovald as the sons of King Chlodomer, specifying that their paternal grandmother took them into her own household after the death of their father[109].  The Liber Hist
2 CONC oriæ Francorum records that "filios…Chlodomire orfanos Theudovaldo, Gunthario et Chlodoaldo" were brought up by "Chrodchildis regina" after their father was killed[110].  In a later passage, Gregory records that the two older sons
2 CONC  were murdered by their uncle King Clotaire, who suspected that his mother was plotting for their succession to the throne, specifying that the older son was 10 years old[111]. [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MEROVINGIANS.htm#Clo
2 CONC visIB MEDLANDS]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>b)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Gunthar-Merovingian/6000000037865140075?through=6000000010395927288 GUNTHAR] ([523]-murdered Paris 531, bur Paris, basilique des Saints-Apôtres [later église de Sainte-Geneviève]).  Greg
2 CONC ory of Tours names (in order) Theudovald, Gunthar and Chlodovald as the sons of King Chlodomer, specifying that their paternal grandmother took them into her own household after the death of their father[112].  The Liber Historiæ 
2 CONC Francorum records that "filios…Chlodomire orfanos Theudovaldo, Gunthario et Chlodoaldo" were brought up by "Chrodchildis regina" after their father was killed[113].  In a later passage, Gregory records that the two older sons were
2 CONC  murdered by their uncle King Clotaire, who suspected that his mother was plotting for their succession to the throne, specifying that the younger son was 7 years old[114]. [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MEROVINGIANS.htm#ClovisI
2 CONC B MEDLANDS]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>c)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Chlodoald-Merovingian/6000000037864811488?through=6000000010395927288 CHLODOVALD] [Cloud] ([524]-7 Sep [560], bur Monastery of Saint-Martin [later Saint-Cloud] near Paris).  Gregory of T
2 CONC ours names (in order) Theudovald, Gunthar and Chlodovald as the sons of King Chlodomer, specifying that their paternal grandmother took them into her own household after the death of their father[115].  The Liber Historiæ Francoru
2 CONC m records that "filios…Chlodomire orfanos Theudovaldo, Gunthario et Chlodoaldo" were brought up by "Chrodchildis regina" after their father was killed[116].  In a later passage, Gregory records that Chlodovald escaped the fate of 
2 CONC his brothers and entered a religious life[117].  He became a monk at Nogent (now Saint-Cloud), near Paris, where he founded the monastery of Saint-Martin, renamed Saint-Cloud by the 8th century.   The Vita Sancti Chlodovaldi recor
2 CONC ds the death of Chlodovald on "VII Id Sep" but does not specify the year[118].  He was canonised as St Cloud, feast day 7 Sep[119]. [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MEROVINGIANS.htm#ClovisIB MEDLANDS]
