2 CONC  Childebert as son of King Clovis and his wife Clotilde, listed after Chlodomer and before Clotaire [120].  "Theodorico, Chlomiro, Hildeberto, Hlodario" are named (in order) as sons of "Chlodoveus" in the Regum Merowingorum Geneal
2 CONC ogia[121].  He succeeded his father in 511 as CHILDEBERT I King of the Franks, at Paris, his territory covering the Seine and Somme valleys as well as the northern coast of France as far as Brittany, Nantes and Angers.  Gregory of
2 CONC  Tours records that King Childebert attacked and defeated Amalric King of the Visigoths [122], which marked the end of the Visigothic government in France and the start of the transfer of their powerbase to Spain.  He and his brot
2 CONC her Clotaire launched a third attack on Burgundy, besieged Autun and occupied the whole kingdom, deposing King Gondemar II [123].  Gregory of Tours records that the childless King Childebert adopted his nephew Theodebert as his he
2 CONC ir after the death of the latter's father [124].  He founded the monastery in Paris which, from the end 11th century, was called Saint-Germain-des-Prés.  Gregory of Tours records the death of King Childebert in Paris and his buria
2 CONC l in the church of St Vincent [125].  The Marii Episcopi Aventicensis Chronica records the death in 558 of "Childebertus rex Francorum"[126].  m [https://www.geni.com/people/Ultragotha/6000000009034387059?through=60000000078152382
