2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Theudebert Merovingian , I
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Wacho or Waccho (probably Waldchis) was king of the Lombards before they entered Italy from an unknown date (perhaps circa 510) until his death in 539. His father was Unichis. Wacho usurped the throne by assassinating (or having a
2 CONC ssassinated) his uncle, King Tato (again, probably around 510). Tato's son Ildchis fought with him and fled to the Gepids where he died.[1] Wacho had good relations with the Franks.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wacho married three times. His first marriage was to Radegund, daughter of Bisinus, King of the Thuringi. His second marriage was to Austrigusa, a Gepid possibly named after her maternal descent from Ostrogothic rulers. Austrigusa
2 CONC  was the mother of two daughters: Wisigarda (who married Theudebert I of Austrasia) and Waldrada (who married firstly Theudebald of Austrasia, secondly Chlothar I, King of the Franks, and thirdly Garibald I of Bavaria). Wacho's th
2 CONC ird marriage was to Silinga, a Heruli-mother of Waltari.
2 CONT
2 CONT A modern descendant is Queen Elizabeth II of the United Kingdom.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT FMG: Gregory of Tours records that Theoderich King of the Franks married the daughter of Sigismond but does not name her [Gregory of Tours III.5, p. 166].  Gregory does not name the mother of King Theoderich´s wife, but chronologi
2 CONC cally it is probable that she was born from King Sigismond's first marriage, which is also suggested by the root "-gotha" in her first name.  Her name is suggested by Flodoard´s history of the church of Reims, dated to the mid-10t
2 CONC h century.  This source records that "Suavegotta regina" bequeathed one third of "ville Virisiaci" by testament to the church of Reims during the bishopric of Bishop Mapinius, subject to the life interest of "Teudichildi prefate r
2 CONC egine filie", adding that the latter later confirmed the donation during the bishopric of Bishop Egidius [Flodoardus Remensis Historia Remensis Ecclesiæ, II, 1, MGH SS XXXVI, p. 132.].  The identification of "Suavegotha regina" as
2 CONC  King Theoderich´s wife depends on the identification of "Teudchildi" as his daughter which, as explained in more detail in the document MEROVINGIAN KINGS, is uncertain.  The link cannot therefore definitively be made between "Sua
2 CONC vegotha" and the daughter of Sigismond King of Burgundy.  Nevertheless, the chronology for such a link is favourable, as the editor of the Monumenta Germaniæ Scriptores edition of Flodoard dates Mapinius´s bishopric to "ca 549-573
2 CONC " and Egidius´s to "ca 573-590".
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
