2 CONT
2 CONT     Pharamond of the Franks of Westph, Possibly a legendary rather than historical figure. Only the later century historicians Prosper Tyron and Dom Bouquet give a report about his reign. In AD 420, he reportedly led his people in
2 CONC  crossing the river Rhine and heading west. This movement would effectively separate his tribe from the majority of the Rhinefranks that had settled near Cologne. Pharamond was eventualy succeeded by his son Clodio.
2 CONT     (From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia)
2 CONT
2 CONT     Pharamond, Duke of the East Franks in 404 A. D., was elected King of the West Franks 419, and is reckoned by historians as the first King of France. He married Argotta, who was descended from Heli, first King of the Britons, o
2 CONC ne of whose descendants had married one of the Kings of France, a daughter Althildis who married Marconier IV, King of France A. D. 128, from whom Argotta was 14th in line. Thus she was 22nd in line from Heli, King of the Britons,
2 CONC  and was called the mother of all the Kings of France.
2 CONT     (Kin of Mellcene Thurman Smith, page 353)
2 CONT
2 CONT     PHARAMOND, King of the West Franks,(*) who died 428, married Argotta, daughter of Gunibald, Duke of the West Franks, who died 419, son of Priam, or Dagobert, first Duke of the West Franks under the Romans, who died 389, son of
2 CONC  Clodius, King of the West Franks 378.
2 CONT     (Fenwick Allied Ancestry, page 58)
