1 NOTE Pharamond
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
2 CONT  </wiki/Image:01_Pharamond.jpg> </wiki/Image:01_Pharamond.jpg>
2 CONT  </wiki/Image:01_Pharamond.jpg> </wiki/Image:01_Pharamond.jpg>Duke Pharamond
2 CONT Pharamond (c.370 </wiki/370> - c.430 </wiki/430>) is considered to be the first Duke </wiki/Duke> of the Salian Franks </wiki/Salian_Franks>, though he is possibly a legendary rather than historical figure. He was possibly a son o
2 CONC r son-in-law of Marcomer </wiki/Marcomer>.
2 CONT Only the later century historicians Prosper Tyron </w/index.php?title=Prosper_Tyron&action=edit> and Dom Bouquet </w/index.php?title=Dom_Bouquet&action=edit> give a report about his reign. In AD 420 </wiki/420>, he reportedly led 
2 CONC his people in crossing the river Rhine </wiki/Rhine> and heading west. This movement would effectively separate his tribe from the majority of the Rhinefranks </w/index.php?title=Rhinefranks&action=edit> that had settled near Colo
2 CONC gne </wiki/Cologne>. Pharamond was eventually succeeded by his son Clodio </wiki/Clodio>. His wife was Argotta </w/index.php?title=Argotta&action=edit>.
