1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.geni.com/people/Chlodomir-I-King-the-Franks-at-Orl%C3%A9ans/6000000010395927288?through=6000000005913350166 CHLODOMER] ([494/95]-killed in battle Vézeronce 21 Jun 524).  Gregory of Tours names Chlodome
2 CONC r as second son of King Clovis and his wife Clotilde[102].  "Theodorico, Chlomiro, Hildeberto, Hlodario" are named (in order) as sons of "Chlodoveus" in the Regum Merowingorum Genealogia[103].  He succeeded his father in 511 as CH
2 CONC LODOMER King of the Franks, at Orléans, his territory covering the Loire valley from Orléans to Tour, Chartres, Sens and Auxerre.  Gregory of Tours records that Chlodomer's mother incited him to attack Burgundy to revenge the deat
2 CONC h of her parents.  He defeated and captured Sigismond King of Burgundy in his first invasion, but was defeated and killed by Sigismond's brother Gondemar during a second invasion[104].  The Liber Historiæ Francorum records that "C
2 CONC hlodomiris" led an army into Burgundy against "Godmarum", a marginal additional recording that "Gladmirus filius Clodovei regis Francorum" was killed during the course of the attack[105].  m ([514] or 521) as her first husband, [h
2 CONC ttps://www.geni.com/people/Guntheuca-of-the-Burgundians-Queen-of-Orl%C3%A9ans/6000000007217837471?through=6000000010395927288 GUNTHEUCA] [Gondioque], daughter of - [King of Burgundy].  Gregory of Tours names Guntheuc as widow of K
2 CONC ing Chlodomer and records her second marriage with his brother Clotaire, but does not give her origin[106].  The Liber Historiæ Francorum records that "Chlotharius" married "uxorem fratris sui…Gundeucam"[107].  Settipani suggests,
2 CONC  for onomastic reasons only, that she may have belonged to the Burgundian royal family which, if correct, means that she may have been the daughter of either King Gondebaud or his brother Godogisel[108].  However, Gregory makes no
2 CONC  mention of this in his lengthy description of King Chlodomer's campaigns in Burgundy, an omission which is surprising if the king’s wife was related to his opponents.  She married secondly ([524]) as his first wife, Clotaire I [C
2 CONC hlothachar/Lothar] King of the Franks.  King Chlodomer & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>a)       ''' [https://www.geni.com/people/Theodebald-Merovingian/6000000037864821289?through=6000000010395927288 THEODEBALD] ([521]-murdered Paris 531, bur Paris, basilique des Saints-Apôtres [later église de Sainte-Geneviève]
2 CONC ).  Gregory of Tours names (in order) Theudovald, Gunthar and Chlodovald as the sons of King Chlodomer, specifying that their paternal grandmother took them into her own household after the death of their father[109].  The Liber H
2 CONC istoriæ Francorum records that "filios…Chlodomire orfanos Theudovaldo, Gunthario et Chlodoaldo" were brought up by "Chrodchildis regina" after their father was killed[110].  In a later passage, Gregory records that the two older s
2 CONC ons were murdered by their uncle King Clotaire, who suspected that his mother was plotting for their succession to the throne, specifying that the older son was 10 years old[111]. [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MEROVINGIANS.htm#
2 CONC ClovisIB MEDLANDS]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>b)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Gunthar-Merovingian/6000000037865140075?through=6000000010395927288 GUNTHAR] ([523]-murdered Paris 531, bur Paris, basilique des Saints-Apôtres [later église de Sainte-Geneviève]). 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>>c)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Chlodoald-Merovingian/6000000037864811488?through=6000000010395927288 CHLODOVALD] [Cloud] ([524]-7 Sep [560], bur Monastery of Saint-Martin [later Saint-Cloud] near Paris). 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/MEROVINGIANS.htm#ClovisIB 
