1 NOTE Dagobert I
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=document&guid=b13552cf-c1f5-4960-9d7e-54039ab8b4f7&tid=8764362&pid=-687688461
1 NOTE hij herenigde een verzwakt koninkrijk, geholpen door de heilige Éloi en de heilige Ouen; hij beschermde de bedreigde grenzen, na 632 alleenheerser.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dagobert I (603-639) was koning der Franken van 629 tot 639.
2 CONT Tussen 623 en 632 was hij koning van Austrasië. In 629 volgde hij zijn vader Chlothar II op als koning der Franken samen met zijn broer Charibert II, die in 632 overlijdt. Tijdens zijn koningschap maakt hij Parijs hoofdstad van he
2 CONC t Frankische rijk. In 623 komt de adel van Austrasië in opstand en moet hij zijn dan nog driejarige zoon Sigibert III koning van Austrasië maken. Zijn zonen zullen, mede door hun schijnkoningschap, bekend worden als de vadsige kon
2 CONC ingen. Dagobert I zelf zal de geschiedenis in gaan als de goede koning.
2 CONT Rise to power
2 CONT
2 CONT Dagobert was the eldest son of Clotaire II and Berthetrude, or possibly Haldetrude. Clotaire II had reigned alone over all the Franks since 613, and Dagobert became the king of Austrasia when her independent nobles demanded a king
2 CONC  of their own. In 623, Clotaire installed his son Dagobert in Austrasia.
2 CONT On the death of his father in 629, Dagobert inherited the Neustrian and Burgundian kingdoms. His half-brother Charibert, son of Sichilde, claimed Neustria but Dagobert opposed him. Brodulf, the brother of Sichilde, petitioned Dago
2 CONC bert on behalf of his young nephew, but Dagobert assassinated him and gave his younger sibling Aquitaine.
2 CONT Charibert died in 632 and his son Chilperic was assassinated on Dagobert's orders. By 632, Dagobert had Burgundy and Aquitaine firmly under his rule, becoming the most powerful Merovingian king in many years and the most respected
2 CONC  ruler in the West.
2 CONT This individual was found on GenCircles at: http://www.gencircles.com/users/robgomes/3/data/11200
2 CONT
2 CONT wissel: 20 april 2006
1 NOTE King of Austrasia.
2 CONT Last Merovingian king to wield any real royal power.
1 NOTE The Life and History of King Dagobert I (Wikipedia)
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=document&guid=03720791-99f2-466d-afe4-0bcf15145c36&tid=6268114&pid=-1057590303
1 NOTE In 623, Dagobert's father, Chlotar II, King of the Franks, made him king
2 CONT of Austrasia to please the leading Austrasian nobles: Mayor of the Palace
2 CONT Pepin I and Saint Arnulf, Bishop of Metz.
2 CONT When Chlotar died in 629, Dagobert became sole King ofthe Franks, and he
2 CONT moved his capital from Austrasia to Paris. Later, Dagobertleft the
2 CONT council of Pepin for a more flexible Neustrian Mayor of the Palace.In
2 CONT 632, he was forced to put his three-year old son Sigebert on the throne
2 CONT of Austrasia as the nobles were in revolt, however Pepin was not made his
2 CONT Mayor of the Palace.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Neustrian nobles then wished to unite with Burgundy, and so they
2 CONT urged Dagobert to put his son Clovis II as king of both those kingdoms,
2 CONT although he was only 5 years old and could be easily manipulated by the
2 CONT nobles. When Dagobert died in 639, the nobles of the kingdoms controlled
2 CONT both his sons, now puppet kings.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dagobert I, King des Francs. Born: in 603, son of Clotaire=Chlothar II, King de Soissons and Bertrude, Some sources assert that Dagobert I was born in the year 606. Note - between 623 and 629: Dagobert I became King of Austrasie i
