1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Anastatasius-Theodora-s-grandson/6000000135524142866?through=6000000003645870259
2 CONT
2 CONT This Anastasius married Juliana - not Joannina.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Juliana’s husband Anastasius is sometimes conflated with Anastasius, husband of Joannina. The marriage year of Joannina and her husband is known, and so the dating of Juliana and her husband Anastasius is sometimes arranged to fit
2 CONC  with a marriage to Joannina.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Probus_(consul_525)_
2 CONT
2 CONT Flavius Probus Iunior (c. 495 – aft. 525) was a Consul of the Ostrogothic Kingdom in 525. He married Proba, daughter of Flavius Olybrius and Irene, a niece of Eastern Roman Emperor Anastasius I. With her he had a daughter, Juliana
2 CONC , who married Anastasius, the son of '''Anastasius Paulus Probus Sabinianus Pompeius Anastasius''', consul in 517.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Information from his father's Wikipedia page: 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anastasius_(consul_517)_
2 CONT
2 CONT Anastasius (c. 530 - aft. 571), married firstly to Joannina, only daughter of General Flavius Belisarius and wife Antonina,[4] a marriage that lasted for eight months when they were forced to separate by her mother and father, wit
2 CONC hout issue ... [this marriage is the other Anastasius, Theodora’s grandson]
2 CONT
2 CONT and married secondly (1st) aft. 548 Juliana (born c. 533), daughter of Flavius Anicius Probus Iunior (c. 495 - aft. 525), consul in 525, and wife and cousin Proba (born c. 510), and had by this second marriage:
2 CONT
2 CONT Placidia (born c. 552), married to John Mystacon (c. 545 - 591),a magister militum per Orientem from 579 to his death in 591, and had issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Areobindus (born c. 550)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anastasius_(consul_517)_
2 CONT * Alan Cameron. Duke University, Greek, Roman and Byzantine Studies The House of Anastasius. Columbia University, pp 259-276. June 1978. Page 270. Accessed 9 April 2020. https://grbs.library.duke.edu/article/viewFile/7451/4919 pag
2 CONC e 17 of PDF Juliana, daughter of Probus & Proba. Wife of Anastatasius (not Theodora’s grandson). Mother of Aerobindus, Proba ( m Georgius), Placidia (m John Mystacon)
