2 CONT Prince Stephanoz (Georgian: სტეფანოზ) was a Georgian prince of the royal Chosroid dynasty. Prince of Kakheti in 685–736.[1][2][3][4]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was son of Prince Adarnase II of Iberia.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had two sons, Prince Archil of Kakheti and Prince Mirian of Kakheti.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen is mentioned in the inscriptions at Ateni Sioni Church dated 735 AD.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT კურთხეული მამფალი სტეფანოზ, ღმერთისა მიერ ქართველთა და მეგრელთა ერისთავთერისთავი უფალი.
2 CONT Blessed Stephen the mampali, by the will of God, the lord and eristavt-eristavi of Georgians and Megrels.
2 CONT
