2 CONT Titel: Kung över frankerna 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT King of Neustria and Burgundy 673; King of Austrasia 676-91
2 CONT
2 CONT d. 690/691 
2 CONT
2 CONT Merovingian ruler who succeeded his brother Chlotar III as king of Neustria and Burgundy in 673, at the instigation of Ebroïn, the Neustrian mayor of the palace. He was soon deposed by another brother, Childeric II, was restored i
2 CONC n 675, then was momentarily deposed again in favour of a certain Clovis (allegedly Chlotar III's son), but recovered his throne in 676 and finally (679) also became king of Austrasia. A puppet pure and simple, he then had to watch
2 CONC  his subjects fight one another until the final victory of Pepin II and the Austrasians at the Battle of Tertry in 687. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Copyright © 1994-2001 Encyclopædia Britannica, Inc.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikipedia:
