2 CONT # ADELPERGA in Biographical Dictionary of Italians - Volume 1 (1960) < [https://www-treccani-it.translate.goog/enciclopedia/adelperga_(Dizionario-Biografico)/?_x_tr_sl=auto&_x_tr_tl=en&_x_tr_hl=en&_x_tr_pto=wapp&_x_tr_hist=true En
2 CONC glish translation] > She was a woman who revealed firmness of character and political shrewdness in the events following her husband's death (August 787); she managed to effectively maintain the independence of the Benevento princ
2 CONC ipality, saving it from the aims of Charlemagne, who allowed Grimoaldo, son of the dead prince, who had been held hostage by him at her court, to regain possession of the principality.
