1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Duke Arichis & his wife had five children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SOUTHERN%20ITALY,%20PRE-NORMAN.htm#Arichisdied787
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         '''ROMOALD''' ( [761/62]-21 Jul 787, bur Salerno Cathedral).  "Rumoldum et Grimoldum" are named as sons of "Aragisus" by Einhard[108].  The Chronicon Salernitanum names (in order) "Romoald, Grimoald et Gisifum, Theodera
2 CONC dam et Adelchisam" as children of Duke Arichis and Adalperga[109].  The Annales Beneventani record the death "pridie Kal Aug 787" of "Roimoaldus filius Arechi", earlier in the same month in which his father died[110].  The Chronic
2 CONC on Salernitanum records that "Romoald filii Arichis" died aged 25[111].  The Annales Laurissenses record the deaths in 787 of "Harichis dux Beneventanus" and of "Romaldum filium suum"[112].  The Annales Laurissenses record the dea
2 CONC ths in 787 of "Harichis dux Beneventanus" and of "Romaldum filium suum"[113].  Einhard records the deaths (in 786) of "Aragisus dux Beneventanorum…Rumoldo maiore filio suo" and the accession of "minore ducis filio Grimoldo"[114]. 
2 CONC  His place of burial is confirmed by the Chronicon Salernitanum which records that his brother "Grimoald" was buried "in…ecclesia sedis Salernitanæ iuxta sepulchra patris fratrisque"[115]. 
