0 @N6000000002187712504@ NOTE Nero
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT For other uses, see Nero (disambiguation). 
1 CONT
1 CONT NeroNero Claudius Caesar Augustus Germanicus (December 15, 37–June 9, 68), born Lucius Domitius Ahenobarbus, also called (50–54) Nero Claudius Drusus Germanicus, was the fifth and last Roman Emperor of the Julio-Claudian dynasty. 
1 CONC On February 25, 50 Nero became heir to the then-Emperor, his grand-uncle and adoptive father Claudius, as Nero Claudius Caesar Drusus, succeeding to the throne on October 13, 54 with Claudius' death. In 66 he added the prefix Impe
1 CONC rator to his name. In 68 Nero was deposed. His subsequent death was reportedly the result of suicide assisted by his scribe Epaphroditos.
1 CONT
1 CONT Contents [hide]
1 CONT 1 Life 
1 CONT 1.1 Family 
1 CONT 1.2 Rise to power 
1 CONT 1.2.1 Birth under Caligula 
1 CONT 1.2.2 Conspiracies 
1 CONT 1.2.3 Adoption by Claudius 
1 CONT 1.3 Emperor 
1 CONT 1.3.1 Becoming Augustus 
1 CONT 1.3.2 A series of scandals 
1 CONT 1.3.3 Disturbed peace and major rebellions 
1 CONT 1.3.4 Great Fire of Rome 
1 CONT 1.3.5 Nero the artist and the widower 
1 CONT 1.3.6 Suicide 
