1 CONC ship; that men ought now to be more circumspect in addressing him, and to regard his word as law. So far did he go in his presumption, that when a soothsayer once reported direful inwards without a heart, he said: "They will be mo
1 CONC re favourable when I wish it; it should not be regarded as a portent, if a beast has no heart..." 
1 CONT ^ His epitaph, written by Sulla himself, has become a common phrase used by those wishing to portray themselves as powerful. It has recently been popularized by Lieutenant General James Mattis as the motto of the 1st Marine Divisi
1 CONC on of the United States Marine Corps: No greater friend, no worse enemy. 
1 CONT ^ Buck, Comparative grammar of Greek and Latin; Latin spelling in the late Republic is variable. 
