1 CONC same disfavour as his father, he fled to Paphlagonia, where he seized Cimiata, a fort at the foot of the Olgassys range. Joined by the Macedonian garrison and by neighbouring populations,he conquered Cappadocian and Paphlagonian t
1 CONC erritories on both sides of the Halys to form the nucleus of his kingdom of Pontic Cappadocia or Pontus. He died in 266/265 B.C., leaving the kingdom to his son Ariobarzanes.
