0 @N6000000002187617604@ NOTE Ariobarzanes of Pontus
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Ariobarzanes (in Greek A??oßa??????; reigned 266–c. 250 BC) was the second king of Pontus, succeeding his father Mithridates I Ctistes in 266 BC and died in an uncertain date between 258 and 240. He obtained possession of the city
1 CONC  of Amastris in Paphlagonia, which was surrendered to him.1 Ariobarzanes and his father sought the assistance of the Gauls, who had come into Asia Minor twelve years before the death of Mithridates, to expel the Egyptians sent by 
1 CONC Ptolemy II Philadelphus.2 Ariobarzanes was succeeded by Mithridates II.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Mithridates I King of Pontus
1 CONT 266 BC – 250 BC Succeeded by:
1 CONT Mithridates II
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT
1 CONT References
