0 @N6000000002187576114@ NOTE She was twenty years old when the Visigoth Alaric attacked Rome and took her prisoner. Four years later she was married to Ataulfo, Alaric's successor, who was later assassinated. She was allowed to leave the 'barbarians' and took
1 CONC  refuge with her brother, Honorius. Aged twenty-seven, she married a general of the empire and succeeded in having him proclaimed co-emperor as Constantius III. When widowed a second time, and after the death of her brother Honori
1 CONC us, she had her own son, Valentinian III, placed on the imperial throne of the west, while she exercised the power of a regent. She died aged sixty and was buried in Rome. Source: Leo van de Pas. Stammtafeln zu Europaeischen Staat
1 CONC en by Prinz von Isenburg. The Roman Emperors 31BC-AD476 by Michael Grant. 
0 @N6000000009304936941@ NOTE #Générale#Faite prisonnière par Alaric en 410, puis epouse de son
