0 @N6000000001876715445@ NOTE Flavius Magnus
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT Flavius Magnus (born ca 390 or 405 ΓÇô 475) was a great personage in Gaul, where he was widely respected for his integrity and practical wisdom. He was a Roman Senator of Narbonne (then Narbo), Consul of Rome with Flavius Apolloni
1 CONC us in 460 and the Prefect of Gaul in 469.
1 CONT His father, born ca 380, might have been the son of Ennodius, Proconsul of Africa. He might have been Flavius Felix (380 ΓÇô 430), Consul of Rome in 428, who married Padusia and was an ancestor of Felix, Consul in 511 (?). His mot
1 CONC her (b. 385) was a daughter of Flavius Julius Agricola, Consul of Rome in 421 and father of Emperor Avitus.
1 CONT He was the father of:
1 CONT * Magnus Felix (430 ΓÇô after 469), a Patron in 469, married to Attica (b. 440), perhaps the parents of:
1 CONT * a son or a daughter (b. 460 or 465), who begot:
1 CONT * Flavius Arcadius Placidus Magnus Felix, Consul of Rome in 511
1 CONT * Araneola (b. 435 or 440), married to Polemius, perhaps them the parents of:
1 CONT * a son or a daughter (b. 460 or 465), who begot:
1 CONT * Flavius Arcadius Placidus Magnus Felix, Consul of Rome in 511
1 CONT * Flavius Probus, a Roman Senator
1 CONT * Ennodius (perhaps) (CRP 458), the father of Cynegia?
1 CONT Sources and references
1 CONT * Sidonius Apollinaris, The Letters of Sidonius (Oxford: Clarendon, 1915), pp. clx-clxxxiii
1 CONT * Christian Settipani, Les Anc├¬tres de Charlemagne (France: ├ëditions Christian, 1989).
1 CONT * Christian Settipani , Continuite Gentilice et Continuite Familiale Dans Les Familles Senatoriales Romaines A L'epoque Imperiale, Mythe et Realite, Addenda I - III (juillet 2000- octobre 2002) (n.p.: Prosopographica et Genealogic
1 CONC a, 2002).
