0 @N6000000002187572843@ NOTE Ferreolus, Senator of Narbonne
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Ferreolus, also called Ferreolus of Rodez (b. 470 or ca 475) was a Senator of Narbonne, then Narbo, who lived in Rodez and was also a Senator there. He was the son of Tonantius Ferreolus and wife Industria.
1 CONT
1 CONT Married firstly ca 531 to a Princess of the Salian Franks, born before 511, daughter of Chlodwig I, without issue,[citation needed] he later married secondly Saint Dode, born before 509, daughter of King Chloderic of the Ripuarian
1 CONC  Franks, he was the father of:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Ansbertus[citation needed]
1 CONT     * Aigulf or Agilulf, Bishop of Metz (590 or 591 – 601)
1 CONT     * Babon
1 CONT     * Deotarius, Bishop of Arisitum
1 CONT     * Ragenfred
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Sources
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Christian Settipani, Les Ancêtres de Charlemagne (France: Éditions Christian, 1989).
1 CONT     * Christian Settipani, Continuite Gentilice et Continuite Familiale Dans Les Familles Senatoriales Romaines A L'epoque Imperiale, Mythe et Realite, Addenda I - III (juillet 2000- octobre 2002) (n.p.: Prosopographica et Genealo
1 CONC gica, 2002).
