0 @N6000000002188305257@ NOTE Agilulf, Bishop of Metz
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Agilulf, also called Aigulf (ca 537 – 601), was a Bishop of Metz between 590 or 591 and 601, and was the predecessor of Arnual or Arnoldus or Arnoald (601–609 or 611). He was a son of Ferreolus, Senator of Narbonne, and wife Dode,
1 CONC  Abbess of Saint Pierre de Reims.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] References
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Christian Settipani, Les Ancêtres de Charlemagne (France: Éditions Christian, 1989).
1 CONT     * Christian Settipani, Continuite Gentilice et Continuite Familiale Dans Les Familles Senatoriales Romaines A L'epoque Imperiale, Mythe et Realite, Addenda I - III (juillet 2000- octobre 2002) (n.p.: Prosopographica et Genealo
1 CONC gica, 2002).
