0 @N6000000002187699503@ NOTE Flavius Probus1
1 CONT b. circa 420, #10489
1 CONT Pedigree 
1 CONT      Flavius Probus was born circa 420.1 He was the son of Flavius Magnus.1 He married Eulalie (?), daughter of Thaumaste I (?), before 450.1,2 He was a man of literary taste and precocious ability.2 He was a friend of Sidonius Ap
1 CONC ollinaris from their schooldays, and husband of Eulalia, a cousin of Sidonius.2  
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT      Child of Flavius Probus and Eulalie (?): 
1 CONT   Industria of Narbonne+   b. c 450 
1 CONT
1 CONT [S175] Christian Settipani, Les Ancêtres de Charlemagne (France: Éditions Christian, 1989). Hereinafter cited as AdC. 
1 CONT [S962] Sidonius Apollinaris, The Letters of Sidonius (Oxford: Clarendon, 1915), pp. clx-clxxxiii; List of Correspondents. Hereinafter cited as Letters of Sidonius (orig.). 
