0 @N6000000001353750052@ NOTE [blended.FTW]
1 CONT [mergebase.FTW]
1 CONT King of the Burgundians 524-534
1 CONT Son of Gundobad, King of the Burgundians, and brother of Sigismund, King of the Burgundians. Godomar and his brother Sigismund were defeated in battle by Clovis' sons and Godomar fled. Sigismund was taken by Chlodomer, King of Orl
1 CONC eans, where he was kept as a prisoner. Godomar then rallied the Burgundian army and won back his kingdom. Meanwhile, Chlodomer ordered the death of Sigismund and marched with his brother Theuderic I, King of Metz, on Burgundy in 5
1 CONC 24. Godomar turned the army in flight, but was persued by the Franks. Chlodomer was killed in the battle. In 534, the Franks killed Gundomar and took over the country of Burgundy.
