0 @N6000000002187726431@ NOTE Marcomer
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Marcomer was a Frankish duke (dux, leader) in the late 4th century. Gregory of Tours mentions him in his Historia Francorum, together with dukes Genobaud and Sunno. Gregory doubts that they were called kings. They crossed the Rhin
1 CONC e, raided the Roman province of Germania and threatened Cologne, in the latter years of Western Roman Emperor Magnus Maximus (c. 388). They reportedly also led the Chatti and the Ampsivarii. Marcomer may have been a predecessor of
1 CONC  the legendary duke Pharamond an ancestor of the Frankish royal dynasty of the Merovingians.
0 @N6000000001744974246@ NOTE Source: Church of JC of the LDS "Ancestral File" CD-Rom database, ver 4.17.
0 @N6000000009304893371@ NOTE #Générale#Profession : Chef franc
