0 @N6000000002187700891@ NOTE Childeric II
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT Merovingian Dynasty Kings of All the Franks 
1 CONT
1 CONT Childeric II (c. 653-673), king of Austrasia, was a son of the Frankish king Clovis II.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 660, although a child, he was proclaimed king of Austrasia, while his brother, Clotaire III, ruled over the rest of the dominions of their father Clovis. After the death of Clotaire in 670, Childeric II became King of all the F
1 CONC ranks - the ruler of all three Frankish kingdoms, Austrasia, Neustria and Burgundy. He was assassinated while hunting in 673, and was buried at St. Germain near Paris.
0 @N6000000002187700881@ NOTE Clotaire III
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Clotaire III (652-673) was the eldest son of Clovis II, king of Neustria and Burgundy. He succeeded his father in his kingdoms in 655 or 658, upon his death. He was under the regency of his mother, Queen Balthild until 664 or 665.
1 CONC  Throughout his reign, he was dominated by his mayor of the palace, Ebroin.
1 CONT
1 CONT Sometime between 657 and 661, he became the ruler of all the Franks through the removal of the usurping Childebert the Adopted, but the Austrasians begged for a king of their own and somtime between 660 and 662, Ebroin gave Austra
1 CONC sia to another son of Clovis II, Clotaire's brother, Childeric II. Clotaire retained Neustria and Burgundy until his death in Spring 673. He was buried in Saint Denis Basilica and a tomb, probably his, was discovered there recentl
1 CONC y. Then, his brother Theuderic III succeeded him.
1 CONT
1 CONT It is notable that he is often described as the first roi fainéant—do-nothing king—of the Merovingian dynasty.
