0 @N6000000002188305313@ NOTE Clovis IV
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Clovis IV (sometimes Clovis III if the other Clovis III is considered an usurper ) (682-695) , son of Theuderic III, was the sole king of the Franks from 691 until his death. Although Clovis IV is called "King of the Franks", he w
1 CONC as really a puppet—a roi fainéant—of Pepin II, mayor of the palace of Austrasia. He assumed the throne at the age of nine and died when he was only thirteen.
1 CONT Clovis IV
1 CONT Merovingian Dynasty
1 CONT Born: 682 Died: 695
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Theuderic III King of the Franks
1 CONT 691–695 Succeeded by
1 CONT Childebert III
0 @N6000000002188305322@ NOTE Childebert III
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Childebert III, called the Just (French: le Juste) (670 or probably 683 – 23 April 711), son of Theuderic III and Clotilda (or Doda) and sole king of the Franks (695-711), he was seemingly but a puppet of the mayor of the palace, 
1 CONC Pepin of Heristal, though his placita show him making judicial decisions of his own will, even against the Arnulfing clan. His nickname has no comprehensible justification except possibly as a result of these judgements, for the L
1 CONC iber Historiae Francorum calls him a "famous man" and "a just man of good memory".
1 CONT
1 CONT He had a son named Dagobert, who succeeded him, as Dagobert III, but his wife was not Edonne, the invention of later fantasists. It is possible, though not likely, that Clotaire IV was also his son. He spent almost his entire life
1 CONC  in a royal villa on the Oise.
1 CONT
1 CONT It was during his reign of sixteen years that, in 708, the bishop of Avranches, Saint Aubert, founded, at the urging of the Archangel Michael, the monastery of Mont-Saint-Michel.
1 CONT
1 CONT Upon his death on April 23, 711, southern Gaul began to grow independent: Burgundy under Bishop Savaric of Auxerre, Aquitaine under Duke Odo the Great, and Provence under Antenor. He was buried in the church of St Stephen at Chois
1 CONC y-au-Bac, near Compiègne.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] External links
1 CONT
1 CONT     * From Merovingians to Carolingians: Dynastic Change in Frankia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Childebert III
1 CONT Merovingian Dynasty
1 CONT Born: 670 Died: 711
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Clovis IV King of the Franks
1 CONT 695–711 Succeeded by
1 CONT Dagobert III
